-- The Universal Credit Regulations 2013 (S.I. 2013/376), Schedules 1 to 5A: layer 2, the seat.
-- Source: ../../registers/source-bundle/uksi-2013-376.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text). Target: the stable build 1.6.98.
--
-- SEAT: a person who claims or receives Universal Credit, alone or as one of a couple, asking whether they are entitled to it, how much, and what they must do or tell the Secretary of State.
--
-- Every question below is an exported rule. It takes plain answers (yes or no, numbers, a nation, one of the module's own named choices) and builds the layer-1 records in its WHERE block; it
-- calls the layer-1 rules and never restates them. A date comes in as a year, a month and a day. A list is built from a count or from a few named entries. Where a layer-1 field is not read by the
-- rule that is called, it is given a placeholder and a comment says so. The questions are grouped under the schedule they come from, in the order of the text.
--
-- The first part of the file holds the builders: small rules that turn a handful of answers into one of the records the Schedule 1 to 5 tests read. A builder's name starts "uc3 seat —".
-- Some answers are carried into several legal limbs on purpose (see NOTES.md, "Seat"): one answer for "my landlord is a local authority" feeds both the local authority limb and the provider
-- of social housing limb of the definitions it appears in; one answer for the nation of Great Britain feeds each of the nation-specific limbs.
--
-- No question here puts a duty on the claimant: this range of the Regulations (Schedules 1 to 5A) states what counts, who is treated as liable, when a home is occupied, how much, and
-- for whom the amounts are worked out. The duties to claim, to report changes and to supply evidence are in other Parts of the Regulations.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- BUILDERS. Each turns the answers a person gives into the record a layer-1 rule takes. A builder decides nothing: it copies an answer into the field it
-- belongs to (or, where one answer stands for several statutory limbs, into each of them), and the rule that is called does all the deciding.
-- Where a person is asked about their home's nation, a statutory test that differs by nation is given the same answer for the limb of every nation, or the limb of
-- the nation they named.

-- A body that may be a local authority: the kind of council that counts depends on the nation, so the answer "it is a local authority" is carried as a county council
-- in England and Wales (which counts in both) and as a council under section 2 of the 1994 Act in Scotland.
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `it is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Body that may be a local authority`
`uc3 seat — a body that may be a local authority` nation `it is a local authority` MEANS
    `Body that may be a local authority` WITH
        `nation of Great Britain in relation to which it is asked` IS nation
        `kind of body` IS
            IF `it is a local authority`
            THEN (CONSIDER nation
                  WHEN England  THEN `a county council`
                  WHEN Wales    THEN `a county council`
                  WHEN Scotland THEN `a council constituted under section 2 of the Local Government etc. (Scotland) Act 1994`)
            ELSE `another kind of body`

-- A charity that may be a registered charity: entered in the register of the nation it is in (Scotland has its own register).
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `it is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Charity that may be a registered charity`
`uc3 seat — a charity that may be a registered charity` nation `it is a registered charity` MEANS
    `Charity that may be a registered charity` WITH
        `entered in the register of charities maintained under Part 4 of the Charities Act 2011` IS IF nation EQUALS Scotland THEN FALSE ELSE `it is a registered charity`
        `entered on the register of charities maintained under the Charities and Trustee Investment (Scotland) Act 2005` IS IF nation EQUALS Scotland THEN `it is a registered charity` ELSE FALSE

-- A body that may be a voluntary organisation.
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `it is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `its activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Body that may be a voluntary organisation`
`uc3 seat — a body that may be a voluntary organisation` nation `it is a public authority` `it is a local authority` `its activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` MEANS
    `Body that may be a voluntary organisation` WITH
        `public authority` IS `it is a public authority`
        `the body as a possible local authority` IS `uc3 seat — a body that may be a local authority` nation `it is a local authority`
        `activities are carried on otherwise than for profit` IS `its activities are carried on otherwise than for profit`

-- Premises that may be a care home: one answer for "it is a care home" stands for the limb of the nation (the rule reads only the nation's own limb);
-- one answer for "it is an independent hospital" stands for the independent-hospital limb of each nation (a health service hospital is not one).
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `it is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Premises that may be a care home`
`uc3 seat — premises that may be a care home` nation `it is a care home` `it is an independent hospital` MEANS
    `Premises that may be a care home` WITH
        `nation of Great Britain in which the premises are` IS nation
        `a care home within the meaning of section 3 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS `it is a care home`
        `a place at which a care home service within the meaning of Part 1 of the Regulation and Inspection of Social Care (Wales) Act 2016 is provided wholly or mainly to persons aged 18 or over` IS `it is a care home`
        `a care home service within the meaning of paragraph 2 of Schedule 12 to the Public Services Reform (Scotland) Act 2010` IS `it is a care home`
        `the premises as a hospital that may be an independent hospital` IS `Hospital that may be an independent hospital` WITH
            `a hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS `it is an independent hospital`
            `a health service hospital as defined by section 275 of the National Health Service Act 2006` IS FALSE
            `an independent hospital as the meaning is assigned to it by section 2 of the Care Standards Act 2000` IS `it is an independent hospital`
            `an independent health care service as defined in section 10F(1)(a) and (b) of the National Health Service (Scotland) Act 1978` IS `it is an independent hospital`

-- A landlord that may be a provider of social housing. The Welsh and Scottish registers of social landlords are one answer, carried to the register of the nation.
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `it is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accommodation is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
`uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` nation `it is a local authority` `it is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `it is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `the accommodation is social housing` `it is a registered social landlord` MEANS
    `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing` WITH
        `the landlord as a possible local authority` IS `uc3 seat — a body that may be a local authority` nation `it is a local authority`
        `non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS `it is a non-profit registered provider of social housing`
        `profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS `it is a profit-making registered provider of social housing`
        `the accommodation is social housing` IS `the accommodation is social housing`
        `the landlord as a possible registered social landlord` IS `Landlord that may be a registered social landlord` WITH
            `registered in the register maintained by the Welsh Ministers under Chapter 1 of Part 1 of the Housing Act 1996` IS (nation EQUALS Wales) AND `it is a registered social landlord`
            `registered in the register maintained by the Scottish Housing Regulator under section 20(1) of the Housing (Scotland) Act 2010` IS (nation EQUALS Scotland) AND `it is a registered social landlord`

-- The home, as the Schedule 1 tests look at it. A tent is a movable structure designed or adapted for sleeping in and not a caravan, mobile home or houseboat.
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `it is a tent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is approved premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is exempt accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests`
`uc3 seat — a home as the Schedule 1 tests look at it` nation `it is a tent` `it is approved premises` `it is a care home` `it is an independent hospital` `it is exempt accommodation` MEANS
    `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests` WITH
        structure IS `Structure that may be a tent` WITH
            `moveable structure` IS `it is a tent`
            `designed or adapted (solely or mainly) for the purpose of sleeping in a place for any period` IS `it is a tent`
            caravan IS FALSE
            `mobile home` IS FALSE
            houseboat IS FALSE
        `approved premises` IS `it is approved premises`
        `care home premises` IS `uc3 seat — premises that may be a care home` nation `it is a care home` `it is an independent hospital`
        `exempt accommodation` IS `it is exempt accommodation`

-- A building that may be a hostel, with the answers about it and about whoever owns or manages it.
GIVEN nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `accommodation is provided otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises` IS A BOOLEAN
      `board is provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `facilities for the preparation of food are provided` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or manager is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or manager is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or manager is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the owner or manager is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `funds are provided by a government department or agency or a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manager is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manager carries on its activities otherwise than for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manager is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building provides care, support or supervision to help residents to be rehabilitated or resettled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Building that may be a hostel`
`uc3 seat — a building that may be a hostel` nation `accommodation is provided otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises` `board is provided` `facilities for the preparation of food are provided` `the owner or manager is a local authority` `the owner or manager is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the owner or manager is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `the building is social housing` `the owner or manager is a registered social landlord` `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis` `funds are provided by a government department or agency or a local authority` `the manager is a public authority` `the manager carries on its activities otherwise than for profit` `the manager is a registered charity` `the building provides care, support or supervision to help residents to be rehabilitated or resettled` `the building is a care home` `the building is an independent hospital` MEANS
    `Building that may be a hostel` WITH
        `domestic accommodation is provided for persons generally or for a class of persons otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises` IS `accommodation is provided otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises`
        `board is provided` IS `board is provided`
        `facilities for the preparation of food adequate to the needs of those persons are provided` IS `facilities for the preparation of food are provided`
        `the owner or manager as a possible provider of social housing` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` nation `the owner or manager is a local authority` `the owner or manager is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the owner or manager is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `the building is social housing` `the owner or manager is a registered social landlord`
        `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis` IS `the building is operated other than on a commercial basis`
        `funds are provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority` IS `funds are provided by a government department or agency or a local authority`
        `the manager as a possible voluntary organisation` IS `uc3 seat — a body that may be a voluntary organisation` nation `the manager is a public authority` `the owner or manager is a local authority` `the manager carries on its activities otherwise than for profit`
        `the manager as a possible registered charity` IS `uc3 seat — a charity that may be a registered charity` nation `the manager is a registered charity`
        `the building provides care, support or supervision with a view to assisting those persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS `the building provides care, support or supervision to help residents to be rehabilitated or resettled`
        `the building as possible care home premises` IS `uc3 seat — premises that may be a care home` nation `the building is a care home` `the building is an independent hospital`

-- The Schedule 1 paragraph 8 facts about a payment, as answered. In a question that does not ask about paragraph 8 they are all FALSE: that question's rules do not read them.
GIVEN `the housing costs element is calculated under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `making the payments is a condition on which the right to occupy the accommodation depends` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are for external cleaning of windows` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the windows are in upper floors of a multi-storey building` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are for other internal or external maintenance or repair of the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are separately identifiable as relating to such maintenance or repair` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are payable by a person who occupies under a shared ownership tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any housing costs element for those payments would be calculated under Schedule 5` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are for the upkeep of areas of communal use` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are for basic services generally available to all persons living in the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are specific to the accommodation and for the use of essential items in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs and charges are of a reasonable amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs and charges are for services or facilities of a description that it is reasonable to provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are for costs for which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are in connection with the use of an asset and transfer it or an interest in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are for food, medical services or personal services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Service charge payment, as paragraph 8 looks at it`
`uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` `the housing costs element is calculated under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5` `making the payments is a condition on which the right to occupy the accommodation depends` `the payments are for external cleaning of windows` `the windows are in upper floors of a multi-storey building` `the payments are for other internal or external maintenance or repair of the accommodation` `the payments are separately identifiable as relating to such maintenance or repair` `the payments are payable by a person who occupies under a shared ownership tenancy` `any housing costs element for those payments would be calculated under Schedule 5` `the payments are for the upkeep of areas of communal use` `the payments are for basic services generally available to all persons living in the accommodation` `the payments are specific to the accommodation and for the use of essential items in it` `the costs and charges are of a reasonable amount` `the costs and charges are for services or facilities of a description that it is reasonable to provide` `the payments are for costs for which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made` `the payments are in connection with the use of an asset and transfer it or an interest in it` `the payments are for food, medical services or personal services` MEANS
    `Service charge payment, as paragraph 8 looks at it` WITH
        `the calculation is made under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5` IS `the housing costs element is calculated under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or under Schedule 5`
        `making the payments is a condition on which the right to occupy the accommodation depends` IS `making the payments is a condition on which the right to occupy the accommodation depends`
        `external cleaning of windows` IS `the payments are for external cleaning of windows`
        `the windows are in upper floors of a multi-storey building` IS `the windows are in upper floors of a multi-storey building`
        `other internal or external maintenance or repair of the accommodation` IS `the payments are for other internal or external maintenance or repair of the accommodation`
        `the payments are separately identifiable as relating to such maintenance or repair` IS `the payments are separately identifiable as relating to such maintenance or repair`
        `the payments are payable by a claimant who occupies accommodation under a shared ownership tenancy` IS `the payments are payable by a person who occupies under a shared ownership tenancy`
        `any amount of housing costs element in respect of those payments would fall to be calculated under Schedule 5` IS `any housing costs element for those payments would be calculated under Schedule 5`
        `ongoing maintenance or cleaning of, and the supply of water, fuel or any other commodity relating to the common use of, internal or external areas, including areas for reasonable facilities` IS `the payments are for the upkeep of areas of communal use`
        `provision, ongoing maintenance, cleaning or repair in connection with basic services generally available to all persons living in the accommodation` IS `the payments are for basic services generally available to all persons living in the accommodation`
        `payments specific to the particular accommodation occupied by the claimant for the use of essential items contained in it` IS `the payments are specific to the accommodation and for the use of essential items in it`
        `the costs and charges to which the payments relate are of a reasonable amount` IS `the costs and charges are of a reasonable amount`
        `the costs and charges relate to services or facilities of such description as it is reasonable to provide` IS `the costs and charges are for services or facilities of a description that it is reasonable to provide`
        `the payments relate to the costs of or charges for providing services or facilities in respect of which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made` IS `the payments are for costs for which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made`
        `the payments are in connection with the use of an asset and result in the transfer of the asset or any interest in it` IS `the payments are in connection with the use of an asset and transfer it or an interest in it`
        `the payments relate to the costs of or charges for providing food, medical services or personal services (including personal care) of any description` IS `the payments are for food, medical services or personal services`

GIVETH A `Service charge payment, as paragraph 8 looks at it`
`uc3 seat — no paragraph 8 facts` MEANS
    `uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A payment that may be a service charge payment, from the answers about what it pays for, and about the home it is paid for.
GIVEN `the payment is for services or facilities for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment is fairly attributable to the cost of providing such services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a qualifying loan under the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 was taken out to make the payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      home IS A `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests`
      facts IS A `Service charge payment, as paragraph 8 looks at it`
GIVETH A `Payment that may be a service charge payment`
`uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` `the payment is for services or facilities for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation` `the payment is fairly attributable to the cost of providing such services or facilities` `a qualifying loan under the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 was taken out to make the payments` home facts MEANS
    `Payment that may be a service charge payment` WITH
        `the payment is, in whole or in part, a payment of, or towards, the costs of or charges for providing services or facilities for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation` IS `the payment is for services or facilities for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation`
        `the payment is, in whole or in part, fairly attributable to the costs of or charges for providing such services or facilities connected with accommodation as are available for the use or benefit of persons occupying accommodation` IS `the payment is fairly attributable to the cost of providing such services or facilities`
        `a qualifying loan within the meaning of regulation 2 of the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 was taken out for the purposes of making the payments` IS `a qualifying loan under the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 was taken out to make the payments`
        `the accommodation occupied by the person for whose use or benefit the services or facilities are provided` IS home
        -- Placeholders: paragraph 7(4) says these three are irrelevant, and no rule reads them.
        `the payments are separately identified as relating to the costs or charges referred to in sub-paragraph (2)` IS FALSE
        `the payments are made in addition to or as part of any other payment` IS FALSE
        `the payments are made under the same agreement as that under which the accommodation is occupied` IS FALSE
        `facts for paragraph 8` IS facts

-- Accommodation that may be specified in paragraph 3A, from the answers about the home, who provides it and why the person is there.
GIVEN home IS A `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests`
      nation IS A `Nation of Great Britain`
      `the provider is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a county council in England for each part of which there is a district council` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a housing association` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider carries on its activities otherwise than for profit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I was admitted in order to meet a need for care, support or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I receive care, support or supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I left my previous home because of domestic violence and the accommodation is provided for that reason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the building is used wholly or mainly for the non-permanent accommodation of persons who have left home because of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      hostel IS A `Building that may be a hostel`
GIVETH A `Accommodation that may be specified in paragraph 3A`
`uc3 seat — a home that may be specified accommodation` home nation `the provider is a local authority` `the provider is a county council in England for each part of which there is a district council` `the provider is a housing association` `the provider is a registered charity` `the provider is a public authority` `the provider carries on its activities otherwise than for profit` `I was admitted in order to meet a need for care, support or supervision` `I receive care, support or supervision` `I left my previous home because of domestic violence and the accommodation is provided for that reason` `the building is used wholly or mainly for the non-permanent accommodation of persons who have left home because of domestic violence` hostel MEANS
    `Accommodation that may be specified in paragraph 3A` WITH
        `the accommodation as it is looked at in the Schedule 1 tests` IS home
        `the provider` IS `Provider of accommodation that may be a relevant body` WITH
            `the provider as a possible local authority` IS `uc3 seat — a body that may be a local authority` nation `the provider is a local authority`
            `council for a county in England for each part of which there is a district council` IS `the provider is a county council in England for each part of which there is a district council`
            `housing association` IS `the provider is a housing association`
            `the provider as a possible registered charity` IS `uc3 seat — a charity that may be a registered charity` nation `the provider is a registered charity`
            `the provider as a possible voluntary organisation` IS `uc3 seat — a body that may be a voluntary organisation` nation `the provider is a public authority` `the provider is a local authority` `the provider carries on its activities otherwise than for profit`
        `the claimant has been admitted into the accommodation in order to meet a need for care, support or supervision` IS `I was admitted in order to meet a need for care, support or supervision`
        `the claimant receives care, support or supervision` IS `I receive care, support or supervision`
        `the accommodation is provided to the claimant because the claimant has left the home as a result of domestic violence` IS `I left my previous home because of domestic violence and the accommodation is provided for that reason`
        `the accommodation consists of a building, or part of a building, which is used wholly or mainly for the non-permanent accommodation of persons who have left their homes as a result of domestic violence` IS `the building is used wholly or mainly for the non-permanent accommodation of persons who have left home because of domestic violence`
        `the accommodation as a building that may be a hostel` IS hostel

-- Accommodation that may be temporary accommodation (paragraph 3B). The last field is not read by the paragraph 3B rules.
GIVEN landlord IS A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
      `the accommodation is exempt accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accommodation is made available to discharge the local authority's functions for homeless people` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accommodation is made available to prevent the person being or becoming homeless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Accommodation that may be temporary accommodation`
`uc3 seat — a home that may be temporary accommodation` landlord `the accommodation is exempt accommodation` `the accommodation is made available to discharge the local authority's functions for homeless people` `the accommodation is made available to prevent the person being or becoming homeless` MEANS
    `Accommodation that may be temporary accommodation` WITH
        `the landlord that rent payments are payable to` IS landlord
        `the accommodation is exempt accommodation` IS `the accommodation is exempt accommodation`
        `the accommodation is made available to the renter to discharge any of the local authority's functions under Part II of the Housing (Scotland) Act 1987, Part VII of the Housing Act 1996 or Part 2 of the Housing (Wales) Act 2014` IS `the accommodation is made available to discharge the local authority's functions for homeless people`
        `the accommodation is made available to the renter to prevent the person being or becoming homeless within the meaning of Part II of the Housing (Scotland) Act 1987, Part VII of the Housing Act 1996 or Part 2 of the Housing (Wales) Act 2014` IS `the accommodation is made available to prevent the person being or becoming homeless`
        -- Placeholder: the paragraph 3B rules do not read this field.
        `the renter is also liable to make service charge payments` IS FALSE

-- Builders for the Schedule 5 and 5A questions, and the ordinary home that the amount questions of Schedules 4 and 5 assume (England; not a tent, approved premises, care home, independent hospital or exempt accommodation).

GIVETH A `Accommodation in the Schedule 1 tests`
`uc3 seat — an ordinary home` MEANS
    `uc3 seat — a home as the Schedule 1 tests look at it` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVETH A `Payment that may be a service charge payment`
`uc3 seat — a service charge payment that meets paragraph 8` MEANS
    `uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` TRUE FALSE FALSE `uc3 seat — an ordinary home` (`uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

GIVETH A `Payment that may be a service charge payment`
`uc3 seat — a payment that is not a service charge payment` MEANS
    `uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` FALSE FALSE FALSE `uc3 seat — an ordinary home` (`uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- A run of assessment periods, each of which counts towards the qualifying period (the person has been receiving universal credit and would otherwise qualify). Paragraph 5(3) makes a period that does not
-- count stop the qualifying period running, so only the run since the last such gap matters. Nothing in paragraph 5 depends on a run longer than 9, so the run built is cut off at 9.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF `Assessment period for the qualifying period`
`uc3 seat — a run of counting assessment periods` n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE (`Assessment period for the qualifying period` WITH
              `the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit in the assessment period` IS TRUE,
              `the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award` IS TRUE)
         FOLLOWED BY (`uc3 seat — a run of counting assessment periods` ((min n 9) MINUS 1))

-- The assessment period in question, which is the last of the periods the qualifying period is counted over. Paragraph 5(1) looks at the periods BEFORE it, so what it holds does not decide the answer.
GIVETH A `Assessment period for the qualifying period`
`uc3 seat — the assessment period in question` MEANS
    `Assessment period for the qualifying period` WITH
        `the owner-occupier has been receiving universal credit in the assessment period` IS TRUE,
        `the owner-occupier would otherwise qualify for the inclusion of an amount calculated under this Schedule in their award` IS TRUE

-- A day before 6 April 2026 on which something was so, if there was one; a day on or after that date on which something was so, if there was one. Schedule 5A compares each such day only with 6 April 2026,
-- so the seat asks yes or no and stands in 5 April 2026 for "a day before" and 6 April 2026 for "a day on or after" (the stand-in day is NOT the claimant's real day).
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` b MEANS
    IF b THEN YMD 2026 4 5 ELSE YMD 2026 4 6

GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DATE
`uc3 seat — a day on or after 6 April 2026 if there was one` b MEANS
    IF b THEN YMD 2026 4 6 ELSE YMD 2026 4 5

-- Builders for the amount questions. These questions take it that what the person pays is a rent payment (or, for a service charge, a service charge payment that meets paragraph 8 where that applies):
-- whether it is one is the answer to the Schedule 1 questions above. The home is taken as an ordinary home in England, not specified or temporary accommodation, so the Schedule 1 classification does not turn on it.

GIVETH A `Landlord that may be a provider of social housing`
`uc3 seat — a landlord that is not a provider of social housing` MEANS
    `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVETH A `Building that may be a hostel`
`uc3 seat — not a hostel` MEANS
    `uc3 seat — a building that may be a hostel` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A payment in respect of accommodation that is a payment of rent in an ordinary home (kind 1), or a service charge payment (kind 2) that meets every paragraph 8 condition where the housing costs
-- element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 (the flag), by way of the communal areas category.
GIVEN `it is a service charge payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 8 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Payment in respect of accommodation`
`uc3 seat — a payment of rent or a service charge payment` `it is a service charge payment` `paragraph 8 applies` MEANS
    `Payment in respect of accommodation` WITH
        description IS `Description of a payment for accommodation` WITH
            `payment of rent` IS NOT `it is a service charge payment`
            `payment for a licence or other permission to occupy accommodation` IS FALSE
            `mooring charge payable for a houseboat` IS FALSE
            `accommodation is a caravan or mobile home and the payment is in respect of the site on which the accommodation stands` IS FALSE
            `contribution towards almshouses` IS `Almshouse contribution` WITH
                `contribution by a resident towards maintaining almshouses (and essential services in them)` IS FALSE
                `the almshouses are provided by a housing association` IS FALSE
                `the housing association as a possible registered charity` IS `uc3 seat — a charity that may be a registered charity` England FALSE
                `the housing association is an exempt charity within Schedule 3 to the Charities Act 2011` IS FALSE
        `the accommodation` IS `uc3 seat — an ordinary home`
        `ground rent` IS FALSE
        `the payment is in respect of the site on which a tent stands` IS FALSE
        `owner-occupier payment within the meaning of Schedule 1 of the Loans for Mortgage Regulations 2017` IS FALSE
        `the payment as a possible service charge payment` IS `uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` `it is a service charge payment` FALSE FALSE `uc3 seat — an ordinary home` (`uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` `paragraph 8 applies` `paragraph 8 applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `paragraph 8 applies` FALSE FALSE `paragraph 8 applies` `paragraph 8 applies` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
        `the accommodation as it may be specified in paragraph 3A` IS `uc3 seat — a home that may be specified accommodation` `uc3 seat — an ordinary home` England FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `uc3 seat — not a hostel`
        `the accommodation as it may be temporary accommodation` IS `uc3 seat — a home that may be temporary accommodation` `uc3 seat — a landlord that is not a provider of social housing` FALSE FALSE FALSE

-- A liability for a payment: the person's answers about it, and one answer ("I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions") carried to each of the three conditions of regulation 25(5).
GIVEN `it is a service charge payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph 8 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      amount IS A NUMBER
      interval IS A `Payment interval`
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total number of payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
`uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` `it is a service charge payment` `paragraph 8 applies` amount interval `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions` `it has already been brought into account` `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` `the total number of payments in the 12 month period` MEANS
    `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation` WITH
        payment IS `uc3 seat — a payment of rent or a service charge payment` `it is a service charge payment` `paragraph 8 applies`
        `amount of each payment in pounds` IS amount
        `how often the payment falls due` IS interval
        `the renter meets the payment condition in respect of the description of relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions`
        `the renter meets the liability condition in respect of the description of relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions`
        `the renter meets the occupation condition in respect of the description of relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions`
        `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different renter` IS `it has already been brought into account`
        `the arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods` IS `the arrangements provide for rent free periods`
        `total number of the relevant payments which the renter is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS `the total number of payments in the 12 month period`

-- A relevant payment in the social rented sector, with the adjustments the person states. A tenant incentive scheme is operated and approved, or not.
GIVEN liability IS A `Liability for a payment in respect of accommodation`
      `the reduction applied under a tenant incentive scheme` IS A NUMBER
      `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing to avoid rent arrears` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount in it that relates to a commodity` IS A NUMBER
      `a rent officer has determined a lower amount` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the lower amount the rent officer determined` IS A NUMBER
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Relevant payment in the social rented sector`
`uc3 seat — a relevant payment in the social rented sector` liability `the reduction applied under a tenant incentive scheme` `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing to avoid rent arrears` `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State` `the amount in it that relates to a commodity` `a rent officer has determined a lower amount` `the lower amount the rent officer determined` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount` MEANS
    `Relevant payment in the social rented sector` WITH
        liability IS liability
        `amount of the reduction applied by a provider of social housing under a tenant incentive scheme` IS `the reduction applied under a tenant incentive scheme`
        scheme IS `Tenant incentive scheme` WITH
            `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions` IS `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing to avoid rent arrears`
            `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State` IS `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State`
        `amount which the Secretary of State is satisfied is included in the relevant payment and relates to the supply to the accommodation of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` IS `the amount in it that relates to a commodity`
        `a rent officer has determined that a landlord might, at the time of the application, reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of the description of relevant payment referred to the rent officer` IS `a rent officer has determined a lower amount`
        `the lower amount determined by the rent officer` IS `the lower amount the rent officer determined`
        `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount`

-- The facts about an under-occupation deduction. The domestic violence and sanctuary scheme answers are the seven facts of paragraph 36(6).
GIVEN `the number of bedrooms in my home` IS A NUMBER
      `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim is not living at the same address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim's circumstances are consistent with domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Facts for the under-occupation deduction`
`uc3 seat — the facts for an under-occupation deduction` `the number of bedrooms in my home` `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies` `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened` `the victim is not living at the same address` `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant` `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` `the victim's circumstances are consistent with domestic violence` `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity` MEANS
    `Facts for the under-occupation deduction` WITH
        `number of bedrooms in the accommodation` IS `the number of bedrooms in my home`
        `regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) applies` IS `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies`
        `domestic violence has been inflicted upon or threatened against the claimant or a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative` IS `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened`
        `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence` IS `the victim is not living at the same address`
        `that person is a qualifying young person and is a dependant of a member of the claimant's extended benefit unit` IS `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant`
        `the claimant provides evidence from a person acting in an official capacity, within the meaning of regulation 98(4), which demonstrates that the claimant is living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` IS `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme`
        `the scheme is a scheme operated by a provider of social housing enabling victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security to the property or the perimeter of the property at which the victim resides` IS `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing`
        `the victim's circumstances are consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them` IS `the victim's circumstances are consistent with domestic violence`
        `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident` IS `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity`

-- A possible close relative, from the two answers: what the other person is to the asker, and what that person's partner is to the asker (limb (b) of "close relative").
GIVEN `the person is related as` IS A `Listed relation`
      `the person's partner is related as` IS A `Listed relation`
GIVETH A `Possible close relative`
`uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person is related as` `the person's partner is related as` MEANS
    `Possible close relative` WITH
        `relation to the person` IS `the person is related as`
        `relation of the partner to the person` IS `the person's partner is related as`

-- A person who may be an owner or director of a company. The person's holding is one holder, the person themself, with the shares and voting rights held together with any
-- associates; a parent undertaking's holdings are not asked (placeholders 0 and FALSE) and the associate test is not read for the person themself.
GIVEN `a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held` IS A NUMBER
      `able to exercise significant influence over the management of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Person who may be an owner or director of a company`
`uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `a director of the company` `the percentage of the shares in the company held` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held` `able to exercise significant influence over the management of the company` MEANS
    `Person who may be an owner or director of a company` WITH
        `is a director of the company` IS `a director of the company`
        `the holdings of the person and the person's associates` IS LIST `Holder of an interest in a company` WITH
            `the holder is the person (A)` IS TRUE
            -- Placeholder: the holder is the person themself, so the associate test is not read.
            `the holder as a possible associate of the person` IS `Person who may be an associate` WITH
                `spouse or civil partner of A` IS FALSE
                `child or step-child of A` IS FALSE
                `age in complete years` IS 0
                `trustee of a settlement under which A has a life interest in possession (in Scotland a life interest)` IS FALSE
                `undertaking of which A is a director` IS FALSE
                `employee or partner of A` IS FALSE
                `has with A an agreement or arrangement with respect to the acquisition, holding or disposal of shares or other interests in X or Y` IS FALSE
                `has with A an agreement or arrangement under which they undertake to act together in exercising their voting power in relation to X or Y` IS FALSE
            `percentage of the shares in C held` IS `the percentage of the shares in the company held`
            `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's shareholding in C` IS `able to exercise significant influence over the management of the company`
            -- Placeholders: a parent undertaking's shares and voting rights are not asked.
            `percentage of the shares in a parent undertaking (P) of C held` IS 0
            `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's shareholding in P` IS FALSE
            `percentage of the voting rights in C that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of` IS `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held`
            `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of C by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in C` IS `able to exercise significant influence over the management of the company`
            `percentage of the voting rights in P that the holder is entitled to exercise, or control the exercise of` IS 0
            `able to exercise a significant influence over the management of P by virtue of the holder's entitlement to exercise, or control the exercise of, voting rights in P` IS FALSE

§ `Universal Credit Regulations 2013 -- Schedules 1 to 5A -- the housing costs element: a claimant's questions`

§§ `Schedule 1 -- what counts as rent and as a service charge`

-- Sch 1 paras 2, 3, 3A, 3B. A "rent payment" for the housing costs element is a payment of a kind listed in paragraph 2 that paragraph 3 does not exclude. The exclusions take in ground rent, a tent
-- or the site of one, approved premises, a care home, an owner-occupier payment under the Loans for Mortgage Regulations 2017, a service charge payment (paragraph 7), "specified accommodation"
-- (paragraph 3A) and "temporary accommodation" (paragraph 3B). Every one of those facts is asked, because the rule reads them all. This question takes it that the housing costs element is not worked out
-- under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5, so the added conditions of paragraph 8 are not asked here: they are in the service charge question below.
@export Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element (Sch 1 paras 2, 3, 3A, 3B)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `what I pay is rent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay a payment of rent?
      `what I pay is for a licence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay for a licence or other permission to occupy your home?
      `what I pay is a mooring charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay a mooring charge for a houseboat?
      `what I pay is for a caravan or mobile home site` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you live in a caravan or mobile home, and is what you pay for the site it stands on?
      `what I pay is an almshouse contribution` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay a resident's contribution towards maintaining almshouses (and essential services in them)?
      `the almshouses are provided by a housing association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the almshouses provided by a housing association?
      `that housing association is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that housing association a registered charity?
      `that housing association is an exempt charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that housing association an exempt charity (within Schedule 3 to the Charities Act 2011)?
      `what I pay is ground rent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay ground rent?
      `what I pay is for the site of a tent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay for the site on which a tent stands?
      `what I pay is an owner-occupier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay an owner-occupier payment within the meaning of Schedule 1 to the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017?
      `my home is a tent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home a tent?
      `my home is approved premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home approved premises?
      `my home is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home a care home?
      `my home is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home an independent hospital?
      `my home is exempt accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home exempt accommodation?
      `what I pay is partly for services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay, in whole or in part, a payment towards the costs of services or facilities for the use or benefit of the people living in your home?
      `what I pay is fairly attributable to services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay, in whole or in part, fairly attributable to the cost of such services or facilities?
      `a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a qualifying loan under the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 taken out to make these payments?
      `my home is provided by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home provided by a local authority?
      `my home is provided by a county council in England with district councils` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home provided by a county council in England, for each part of which there is a district council?
      `my home is provided by a housing association` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home provided by a housing association?
      `my home is provided by a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home provided by a registered charity?
      `my home is provided by a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home provided by a public authority?
      `my home is provided by a body not run for profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the body that provides your home carry on its activities otherwise than for profit?
      `I was admitted to my home to meet a need for care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you admitted into your home in order to meet a need for care, support or supervision?
      `I receive care in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you receive care, support or supervision in your home?
      `I left home because of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home provided to you because you left your previous home as a result of domestic violence?
      `my home is in a building for people who left home because of domestic violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home in a building (or part of a building) used wholly or mainly for the non-permanent accommodation of people who have left their homes as a result of domestic violence?
      `the building has accommodation that is not self-contained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home in a building where domestic accommodation is provided for people generally, or for a class of people, otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises?
      `the building provides board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide board?
      `the building provides facilities for preparing food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide facilities for preparing food adequate to the needs of those people?
      `the building is owned or managed by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building owned or managed by a local authority?
      `the building is owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `the building is owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `the building is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building social housing?
      `the building is owned or managed by a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `the building is not run on a commercial basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building operated other than on a commercial basis?
      `the building is funded by government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are funds for the building provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority?
      `the building's manager is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manager of the building a public authority?
      `the building's manager is not run for profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the manager of the building carry on its activities otherwise than for profit?
      `the building's manager is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manager of the building a registered charity?
      `the building helps residents to be resettled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide care, support or supervision with a view to helping the people there to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the building is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building a care home?
      `the building is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building an independent hospital?
      `my landlord is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord you pay rent to a local authority?
      `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `my home is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home social housing?
      `my landlord is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `my home is made available for homeless people under a duty of the local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home made available to you to discharge any of the local authority's functions for homeless people (under Part II of the Housing (Scotland) Act 1987, Part VII of the Housing Act 1996 or Part 2 of the Housing (Wales) Act 2014)?
      `my home is made available to prevent my homelessness` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home made available to you to prevent you being or becoming homeless (within the meaning of those Acts)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does what I pay for my home count as rent for the housing costs element` IF
    `Sch 1 para 2 — a rent payment` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `Payment in respect of accommodation` WITH
            description IS `Description of a payment for accommodation` WITH
                `payment of rent` IS `what I pay is rent`
                `payment for a licence or other permission to occupy accommodation` IS `what I pay is for a licence`
                `mooring charge payable for a houseboat` IS `what I pay is a mooring charge`
                `accommodation is a caravan or mobile home and the payment is in respect of the site on which the accommodation stands` IS `what I pay is for a caravan or mobile home site`
                `contribution towards almshouses` IS `Almshouse contribution` WITH
                    `contribution by a resident towards maintaining almshouses (and essential services in them)` IS `what I pay is an almshouse contribution`
                    `the almshouses are provided by a housing association` IS `the almshouses are provided by a housing association`
                    `the housing association as a possible registered charity` IS `uc3 seat — a charity that may be a registered charity` `my home is in` `that housing association is a registered charity`
                    `the housing association is an exempt charity within Schedule 3 to the Charities Act 2011` IS `that housing association is an exempt charity`
            `the accommodation` IS `my home`
            `ground rent` IS `what I pay is ground rent`
            `the payment is in respect of the site on which a tent stands` IS `what I pay is for the site of a tent`
            `owner-occupier payment within the meaning of Schedule 1 of the Loans for Mortgage Regulations 2017` IS `what I pay is an owner-occupier payment`
            `the payment as a possible service charge payment` IS `uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` `what I pay is partly for services or facilities` `what I pay is fairly attributable to services or facilities` `a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay` `my home` `uc3 seat — no paragraph 8 facts`
            `the accommodation as it may be specified in paragraph 3A` IS `uc3 seat — a home that may be specified accommodation` `my home` `my home is in` `my home is provided by a local authority` `my home is provided by a county council in England with district councils` `my home is provided by a housing association` `my home is provided by a registered charity` `my home is provided by a public authority` `my home is provided by a body not run for profit` `I was admitted to my home to meet a need for care` `I receive care in my home` `I left home because of domestic violence` `my home is in a building for people who left home because of domestic violence` `the building I live in`
            `the accommodation as it may be temporary accommodation` IS `uc3 seat — a home that may be temporary accommodation` `my landlord` `my home is exempt accommodation` `my home is made available for homeless people under a duty of the local authority` `my home is made available to prevent my homelessness`
        `my home` MEANS `uc3 seat — a home as the Schedule 1 tests look at it` `my home is in` `my home is a tent` `my home is approved premises` `my home is a care home` `my home is an independent hospital` `my home is exempt accommodation`
        `the building I live in` MEANS `uc3 seat — a building that may be a hostel` `my home is in` `the building has accommodation that is not self-contained` `the building provides board` `the building provides facilities for preparing food` `the building is owned or managed by a local authority` `the building is owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the building is owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `the building is social housing` `the building is owned or managed by a registered social landlord` `the building is not run on a commercial basis` `the building is funded by government` `the building's manager is a public authority` `the building's manager is not run for profit` `the building's manager is a registered charity` `the building helps residents to be resettled` `the building is a care home` `the building is an independent hospital`
        `my landlord` MEANS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` `my home is in` `my landlord is a local authority` `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `my home is social housing` `my landlord is a registered social landlord`

-- Sch 1 paras 7 and 8. A "service charge payment" is a payment towards the cost of services or facilities for people living in the accommodation, unless a qualifying mortgage-interest loan was
-- taken out for it or it is for a tent, approved premises, a care home or exempt accommodation. When the housing costs element is calculated under Part 5 of Schedule 4 (social rented
-- sector) or under Schedule 5 (owner-occupiers), paragraph 8 adds four conditions: a right-to-occupy condition, a category of payment, a reasonableness condition and an exclusion condition.
@export Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element (Sch 1 paras 7, 8)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `what I pay is partly for services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay, in whole or in part, a payment towards the costs of services or facilities for the use or benefit of the people living in your home?
      `what I pay is fairly attributable to services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay, in whole or in part, fairly attributable to the cost of such services or facilities?
      `a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a qualifying loan under the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 taken out to make these payments?
      `my home is a tent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home a tent?
      `my home is approved premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home approved premises?
      `my home is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home a care home?
      `my home is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home an independent hospital?
      `my home is exempt accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home exempt accommodation?
      `my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your housing costs element worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 (you rent from a social landlord) or under Schedule 5 (you own your home)?
      `the right to occupy depends on making the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is making these payments a condition on which your right to occupy your home depends?
      `the payments are for external window cleaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for the external cleaning of windows?
      `the windows are in upper floors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the windows in the upper floors of a multi-storey building?
      `the payments are for other maintenance or repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for other internal or external maintenance or repair of your home?
      `the payments for repair are separately identifiable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments separately identifiable as relating to that maintenance or repair?
      `I occupy under a shared ownership tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy your home under a shared ownership tenancy?
      `my housing costs element for these payments is calculated under Schedule 5` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would any housing costs element for these payments be calculated under Schedule 5?
      `the payments are for communal areas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for ongoing maintenance or cleaning of, or the supply of water, fuel or any other commodity to, internal or external areas of communal use (including reasonable facilities such as laundry rooms or children's play areas)?
      `the payments are for basic communal services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for the provision, ongoing maintenance, cleaning or repair of basic services available to everyone living in the accommodation (such as refuse collection, communal lifts, secure building access or aerials)?
      `the payments are for essential items in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments specific to your home and limited to the use of essential items in it (such as furniture or domestic appliances)?
      `the costs are of a reasonable amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs and charges the payments relate to of a reasonable amount?
      `the services are of a reasonable description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the costs and charges relate to services or facilities of a description that it is reasonable to provide?
      `public funds might otherwise pay for the services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the payments relate to services or facilities for which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made?
      `the payments transfer an asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments in connection with the use of an asset and do they result in the transfer of the asset or any interest in it?
      `the payments are for food or medical or personal services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the payments relate to the cost of providing food, medical services or personal services (including personal care)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I pay a service charge payment for the housing costs element` IF
    `Sch 1 para 7(1) — a service charge payment` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` `what I pay is partly for services or facilities` `what I pay is fairly attributable to services or facilities` `a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay` `my home` `the paragraph 8 facts`
        `my home` MEANS `uc3 seat — a home as the Schedule 1 tests look at it` `my home is in` `my home is a tent` `my home is approved premises` `my home is a care home` `my home is an independent hospital` `my home is exempt accommodation`
        `the paragraph 8 facts` MEANS `uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` `my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 or Schedule 5` `the right to occupy depends on making the payments` `the payments are for external window cleaning` `the windows are in upper floors` `the payments are for other maintenance or repair` `the payments for repair are separately identifiable` `I occupy under a shared ownership tenancy` `my housing costs element for these payments is calculated under Schedule 5` `the payments are for communal areas` `the payments are for basic communal services` `the payments are for essential items in my home` `the costs are of a reasonable amount` `the services are of a reasonable description` `public funds might otherwise pay for the services` `the payments transfer an asset` `the payments are for food or medical or personal services`

§§ `Schedule 2 -- who is treated as liable to make the payments`

-- Sch 2 paras 1 to 4. A claimant who is not liable in fact may be treated as liable: because the person who is liable is a child or qualifying young person they are responsible for, or
-- (for a single claimant who is a member of a couple, other than by regulation 3(4)) their partner; because the person who is liable has failed to pay and the claimant must pay to stay in the home
-- (all four conditions of paragraph 2); because a liability was waived for repair or re-decoration work the landlord would otherwise have done; and for the whole of a rent free period.
@export Am I liable to make the payments, or treated as liable (Sch 2 paras 1 to 4)?
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2` @desc What kind of payment is it? (rent payments, service charge payments or owner-occupier payments)
      `I am liable in fact` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your tenancy, licence or agreement make you liable to make the payments?
      `the person who is liable is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who is liable to make the payments a child or qualifying young person for whom you (or your partner) are responsible?
      `the person who is liable is my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who is liable to make the payments the other member of the couple you are a member of?
      `my claim basis` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Are you claiming as a single claimant, as one of joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `I am claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)?
      `the person who is liable is not making the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who is liable to make the payments not doing so?
      `I have to make the payments to stay in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have to make the payments in order to continue to live in your home?
      `it would be unreasonable to expect me to make other arrangements` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your circumstances such that it would be unreasonable to expect you to make other arrangements?
      `it is otherwise reasonable to treat me as liable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it otherwise reasonable, in all the circumstances, to treat you as liable to make the payments?
      `the liability to make the payments has been waived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person you owe the payments to waived your liability to make them?
      `the waiver is compensation for repair or re-decoration I carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the waiver by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works you carried out to your home?
      `the works are works the landlord would otherwise have carried out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are they works that the person you owe the payments to would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out?
      `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods?
      `this is a period in which I have no liability to make one or more of the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period you are asking about one in which you have no liability to make one or more of the payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I liable to make the payments or treated as liable under Part 1 of Schedule 2` IF
    `Sch 2 — the claimant is liable in fact or treated as liable under Part 1` `my Part 1 facts` `the kind of payment`
    WHERE
        `my Part 1 facts` MEANS `Part 1 facts about a liability` WITH
            `the claimant is liable in fact` IS `I am liable in fact`
            `the person who is liable` IS `Person who is liable to make the payments` WITH
                `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, either member) is responsible` IS `the person who is liable is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS `the person who is liable is my partner`
            `claim basis` IS `my claim basis`
            `claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)` IS `I am claiming as a single person by virtue of regulation 3(4)`
            `failure to pay` IS `Failure to pay by the person who is liable` WITH
                `the person who is liable to make the payments is not doing so` IS `the person who is liable is not making the payments`
                `the claimant has to make the payments in order to continue occupation of the accommodation` IS `I have to make the payments to stay in my home`
                `the claimant's circumstances are such that it would be unreasonable to expect them to make other arrangements` IS `it would be unreasonable to expect me to make other arrangements`
                `it is otherwise reasonable in all the circumstances to treat the claimant as liable to make the payments` IS `it is otherwise reasonable to treat me as liable`
            waiver IS `Waiver of liability for repair work` WITH
                `the liability to make payments is waived by the person to whom the liability is owed` IS `the liability to make the payments has been waived`
                `the waiver is by way of reasonable compensation for reasonable repair or re-decoration works carried out by the claimant to the accommodation` IS `the waiver is compensation for repair or re-decoration I carried out`
                `the works are works which the person to whom the liability is owed would otherwise have carried out or been required to carry out` IS `the works are works the landlord would otherwise have carried out`
            `the arrangements provide for rent free periods` IS `the arrangements provide for rent free periods`
            `the period` IS `Period of the arrangements` WITH
                `the renter has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the relevant payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 6` IS `this is a period in which I have no liability to make one or more of the payments`


-- Sch 2 paras 5 to 8. A claimant is treated as NOT liable to make rent payments (paragraph 5) to a person who lives in the accommodation and is their partner, a child or qualifying young person
-- they are responsible for, or a close relative of any of them; (paragraph 6) to a company of which a listed person is an owner or director; (paragraph 7) to a trustee of a trust of which a listed person is a
-- trustee or beneficiary; and (paragraph 8) owner-occupier payments to a person in the household. For service charge payments the treatment follows only where it applies to the rent or owner-occupier
-- payments to the same person.
@export Am I treated as not liable to make the payments (Sch 2 paras 5 to 8)?
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2` @desc What kind of payment is it? (rent payments, service charge payments or owner-occupier payments)
      `the person I pay lives in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person you pay live in your home?
      `the person I pay is my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you pay the other member of the couple you are a member of?
      `the person I pay is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you pay a child or qualifying young person for whom you (or your partner) are responsible?
      `the person I pay is related to me as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the person you pay related to you? (a parent, a parent-in-law, a son, a son-in-law, a daughter, a daughter-in-law, a step-parent, a step-son, a step-daughter, a brother, a sister, or not a listed relation)
      `the partner of the person I pay is related to me as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the person you pay is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to you? (the same list)
      `the person I pay is related to my partner as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the person you pay related to your partner? (the same list)
      `the partner of the person I pay is related to my partner as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the person you pay is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to your partner? (the same list)
      `the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the person you pay related to the child or qualifying young person you are responsible for? (the same list)
      `the partner of the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the person you pay is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to that child or qualifying young person? (the same list)
      `I am treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person?
      `I am a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by you, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by me and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by you, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `I and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `my partner is a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by my partner and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by your partner, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by my partner and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by your partner, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `my partner and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your partner, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `the child or qualifying young person is a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the qualifying young person you are responsible for a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by the qualifying young person you are responsible for, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by the qualifying young person you are responsible for, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the child or qualifying young person and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the qualifying young person you are responsible for, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `the close relative is a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the close relative and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the close relative and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the close relative and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `that close relative is related as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is that close relative related to the person they are a relative of? (the same list)
      `the partner of that close relative is related as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If that close relative is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to that person? (the same list)
      `that close relative lives in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that close relative live in your home with you?
      `I am treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company?
      `the payments are owed to a trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments owed to a trustee of a trust?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the trustees or beneficiaries of the trust include you?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they include your partner?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they include a child or qualifying young person for whom you or your partner are responsible?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative living in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they include a close relative of any of those people who lives in your home with you?
      `I am treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust?
      `the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments owed to a person who lives in your household?
      `I am treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person?
      `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not liable to make the payments because of who I owe them to` IF
    `Sch 2 paras 5 to 8 — the claimant is treated as not liable to make the payments` `my facts`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment`
            `the creditor as a possible person within paragraph 5` IS `Person to whom a liability is owed` WITH
                `the person lives in the accommodation` IS `the person I pay lives in my home`
                `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS `the person I pay is my partner`
                `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member) is responsible` IS `the person I pay is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                `the person as a possible close relative of the claimant` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person I pay is related to me as` `the partner of the person I pay is related to me as`
                `the person as a possible close relative of the other member of the couple` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person I pay is related to my partner as` `the partner of the person I pay is related to my partner as`
                `the person as a possible close relative of a child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b)` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as` `the partner of the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as`
            `the creditor as a possible company` IS `Company to which a liability is owed` WITH
                `the claimant as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `I am a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by me and associates` `I and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `the other member of the couple as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `my partner is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by my partner and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by my partner and associates` `my partner and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `a qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible, as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `the child or qualifying young person is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` `the child or qualifying young person and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `a close relative of any of the above, as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `the close relative is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the close relative and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the close relative and associates` `the close relative and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `the close relative as a possible close relative` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `that close relative is related as` `the partner of that close relative is related as`
                `the close relative lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS `that close relative lives in my home`
            `the creditor as a possible trust` IS `Trust to which a liability is owed` WITH
                `the liability is owed to a trustee of a trust` IS `the payments are owed to a trustee of a trust`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include me`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include the other member of the couple` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include my partner`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative living in my home`
            `the creditor as a possible household member` IS `Household creditor` WITH
                `the liability is owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household` IS `the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person` IS `I am treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company` IS `I am treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust` IS `I am treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person` IS `I am treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person`
            `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments` IS `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments`

-- Sch 2 para 9. Where the claimant is not treated as not liable under paragraphs 5 to 8, the amount of an increase in the sum otherwise payable that results from arrears or any other unpaid
-- liability is an amount for which the claimant is treated as not liable. Where they are, the paragraph makes no difference to what they owe, and the rule gives 0.
