                `the claimant as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `I am a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by me and associates` `I and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `the other member of the couple as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `my partner is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by my partner and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by my partner and associates` `my partner and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `a qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible, as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `the child or qualifying young person is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` `the child or qualifying young person and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `a close relative of any of the above, as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `the close relative is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the close relative and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the close relative and associates` `the close relative and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `the close relative as a possible close relative` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `that close relative is related as` `the partner of that close relative is related as`
                `the close relative lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS `that close relative lives in my home`
            `the creditor as a possible trust` IS `Trust to which a liability is owed` WITH
                `the liability is owed to a trustee of a trust` IS `the payments are owed to a trustee of a trust`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include me`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include the other member of the couple` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include my partner`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative living in my home`
            `the creditor as a possible household member` IS `Household creditor` WITH
                `the liability is owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household` IS `the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person` IS `I am treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company` IS `I am treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust` IS `I am treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person` IS `I am treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person`
            `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments` IS `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments`

-- Sch 2 para 10. Where the Secretary of State is satisfied that the liability was contrived in order to secure the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award or to increase its amount,
-- the claimant is treated as not liable (unless already treated as not liable under paragraphs 5 to 8).
@export Am I treated as not liable because my liability was contrived (Sch 2 para 10)?
GIVEN `the kind of payment` IS A `Kind of payment under Schedule 2` @desc What kind of payment is it? (rent payments, service charge payments or owner-occupier payments)
      `the person I pay lives in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person you pay live in your home?
      `the person I pay is my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you pay the other member of the couple you are a member of?
      `the person I pay is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you pay a child or qualifying young person for whom you (or your partner) are responsible?
      `the person I pay is related to me as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the person you pay related to you? (a parent, a parent-in-law, a son, a son-in-law, a daughter, a daughter-in-law, a step-parent, a step-son, a step-daughter, a brother, a sister, or not a listed relation)
      `the partner of the person I pay is related to me as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the person you pay is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to you? (the same list)
      `the person I pay is related to my partner as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the person you pay related to your partner? (the same list)
      `the partner of the person I pay is related to my partner as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the person you pay is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to your partner? (the same list)
      `the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is the person you pay related to the child or qualifying young person you are responsible for? (the same list)
      `the partner of the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If the person you pay is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to that child or qualifying young person? (the same list)
      `I am treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person?
      `I am a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by you, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by me and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by you, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `I and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can you, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `my partner is a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your partner a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by my partner and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by your partner, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by my partner and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by your partner, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `my partner and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can your partner, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `the child or qualifying young person is a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the qualifying young person you are responsible for a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by the qualifying young person you are responsible for, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by the qualifying young person you are responsible for, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the child or qualifying young person and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can the qualifying young person you are responsible for, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `the close relative is a director of the company I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person a director of the company you pay?
      `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the close relative and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the shares in the company is held by a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the close relative and associates` IS A NUMBER @desc What percentage of the voting rights in the company is held by a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person, together with any associates? (0 if none)
      `the close relative and associates can exercise significant influence over the company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Can a close relative of yours, your partner or that young person, together with any associates, exercise significant influence over the management of the company through their holdings?
      `that close relative is related as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc How is that close relative related to the person they are a relative of? (the same list)
      `the partner of that close relative is related as` IS A `Listed relation` @desc If that close relative is a member of a couple, how is their partner related to that person? (the same list)
      `that close relative lives in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does that close relative live in your home with you?
      `I am treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company?
      `the payments are owed to a trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments owed to a trustee of a trust?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the trustees or beneficiaries of the trust include you?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include my partner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they include your partner?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they include a child or qualifying young person for whom you or your partner are responsible?
      `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative living in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do they include a close relative of any of those people who lives in your home with you?
      `I am treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust?
      `the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments owed to a person who lives in your household?
      `I am treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person?
      `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is there no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that my liability was contrived` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that the liability to make the payments was contrived in order to secure the inclusion of the housing costs element in your award of universal credit, or to increase the amount of that element?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as not liable because my liability was contrived` IF
    `Sch 2 para 10 — the claimant is treated as not liable because the liability was contrived` `my facts` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that my liability was contrived`
    WHERE
        `my facts` MEANS `Facts about a liability, as Part 2 reads them` WITH
            `kind of payment` IS `the kind of payment`
            `the creditor as a possible person within paragraph 5` IS `Person to whom a liability is owed` WITH
                `the person lives in the accommodation` IS `the person I pay lives in my home`
                `the other member of the couple of which the claimant is a member` IS `the person I pay is my partner`
                `a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant (or if the claimant is a member of a couple, the other member) is responsible` IS `the person I pay is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                `the person as a possible close relative of the claimant` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person I pay is related to me as` `the partner of the person I pay is related to me as`
                `the person as a possible close relative of the other member of the couple` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person I pay is related to my partner as` `the partner of the person I pay is related to my partner as`
                `the person as a possible close relative of a child or qualifying young person who falls within paragraph (b)` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as` `the partner of the person I pay is related to the child or qualifying young person as`
            `the creditor as a possible company` IS `Company to which a liability is owed` WITH
                `the claimant as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `I am a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by me and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by me and associates` `I and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `the other member of the couple as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `my partner is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by my partner and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by my partner and associates` `my partner and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `a qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible, as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `the child or qualifying young person is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the child or qualifying young person and associates` `the child or qualifying young person and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `a close relative of any of the above, as a possible owner or director` IS `uc3 seat — a person who may be an owner or director of a company` `the close relative is a director of the company I pay` `the percentage of the shares in the company held by the close relative and associates` `the percentage of the voting rights in the company held by the close relative and associates` `the close relative and associates can exercise significant influence over the company`
                `the close relative as a possible close relative` IS `uc3 seat — a possible close relative` `that close relative is related as` `the partner of that close relative is related as`
                `the close relative lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS `that close relative lives in my home`
            `the creditor as a possible trust` IS `Trust to which a liability is owed` WITH
                `the liability is owed to a trustee of a trust` IS `the payments are owed to a trustee of a trust`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include the claimant` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include me`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include the other member of the couple` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include my partner`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant or the other member is responsible` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative of any of the above who lives in the accommodation with the claimant` IS `the trustees or beneficiaries include a close relative living in my home`
            `the creditor as a possible household member` IS `Household creditor` WITH
                `the liability is owed to a person who lives in the claimant's household` IS `the payments are owed to a person who lives in my household`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person` IS `I am treated under paragraph 5(1) as not liable to make rent payments to that person`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company` IS `I am treated under paragraph 6(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a company`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust` IS `I am treated under paragraph 7(1) as not liable to make rent payments to a trustee of a trust`
            `the claimant is treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person` IS `I am treated under paragraph 8(1) as not liable to make owner-occupier payments to that person`
            `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments` IS `there is no liability to make rent payments or owner-occupier payments`

§§ `Schedule 3 -- when a claimant is treated as occupying a home`

-- Sch 3 para 1. A claimant is treated as occupying as their home the accommodation they normally occupy as their home, but, subject to the later paragraphs of Part 1 of the Schedule, not accommodation that
-- comprises more than one dwelling (paragraph 1(2)). Which of several dwellings is the one normally occupied is a matter of all the circumstances (paragraph 1(3)), and is the answer to the first question.
@export Is the accommodation I normally live in treated as my home (Sch 3 para 1)?
GIVEN `this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the accommodation you normally occupy as your home?
      `the number of dwellings my accommodation comprises` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dwellings does your accommodation comprise?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is the accommodation I normally live in treated as my home` IF
    `Sch 3 para 1 — the claimant is treated as occupying the accommodation as their home` `my accommodation`
    WHERE
        `my accommodation` MEANS `Accommodation the claimant may occupy as their home` WITH
            `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS `this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home`
            `number of dwellings the accommodation comprises` IS `the number of dwellings my accommodation comprises`


-- Sch 3 para 2. Where the home is on or pertains to a croft, and the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation, the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation.
@export Is my croft land treated as part of my home (Sch 3 para 2)?
GIVEN `this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the accommodation you normally occupy as your home?
      `my accommodation is on or pertains to a croft` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your accommodation situated on, or does it pertain to, a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993?
      `the croft land is used for the purposes of my accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the croft land used for the purposes of your accommodation?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my croft land treated as part of my home` IF
    `Sch 3 para 2 — the croft land is treated as included in the accommodation` `my accommodation`
    WHERE
        `my accommodation` MEANS `Accommodation that may be on a croft` WITH
            `the accommodation is the accommodation which the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS `this is the accommodation I normally occupy as my home`
            `the accommodation is situated on or pertains to a croft within the meaning of section 3(1) of the Crofters (Scotland) Act 1993` IS `my accommodation is on or pertains to a croft`
            `the croft land is used for the purposes of the accommodation` IS `the croft land is used for the purposes of my accommodation`


-- Sch 3 para 3. A claimant who has to move out of their home for essential repairs and intends to return is treated as normally occupying the other accommodation, or the accommodation under repair,
-- according to which of them they meet the payment and liability conditions for; if they meet them for both, or for neither, the general rule in paragraph 1 applies.
@export Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired (Sch 3 para 3)?
GIVEN `I have to move into other accommodation because of essential repairs to my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you required to move into other accommodation on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation you normally occupy as your home?
      `I intend to return to the home under repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to return to the accommodation that is under repair?
      `I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for the other accommodation?
      `I meet the payment and liability conditions for the home under repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for the accommodation you normally occupy as your home?
GIVETH A `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 3`
DECIDE `Which home am I treated as normally occupying while my home is being repaired` IS
    `Sch 3 para 3 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` `my move for repairs`
    WHERE
        `my move for repairs` MEANS `Claimant living in other accommodation during essential repairs` WITH
            `the claimant is required to move into the other accommodation on account of essential repairs being carried out to the accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` IS `I have to move into other accommodation because of essential repairs to my home`
            `the claimant intends to return to the accommodation which is under repair` IS `I intend to return to the home under repair`
            `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation` IS `I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation`
            `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home` IS `I meet the payment and liability conditions for the home under repair`


-- Sch 3 para 4. A claimant housed by a provider of social housing in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with them, who normally occupies both with
-- them and meets the payment and liability conditions for both, is treated as normally occupying both as a single accommodation.
@export Am I treated as occupying both my dwellings as one home (Sch 3 para 4)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `my landlord is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord who housed you a local authority?
      `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `my home is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your accommodation social housing?
      `my landlord is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `I have been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with you?
      `I normally occupy both dwellings with children or qualifying young persons I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you normally occupy both dwellings, accommodation A and accommodation B, with children or qualifying young persons for whom you are responsible?
      `I meet the payment and liability conditions for accommodation A` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for accommodation A?
      `I meet the payment and liability conditions for accommodation B` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for accommodation B?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as occupying both my dwellings as one home` IF
    `Sch 3 para 4 — both dwellings are treated as the single accommodation the claimant normally occupies as their home` `my two dwellings`
    WHERE
        `my two dwellings` MEANS `Claimant housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing` WITH
            `the provider of social housing that housed the claimant` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` `my home is in` `my landlord is a local authority` `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `my home is social housing` `my landlord is a registered social landlord`
            `the claimant has been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with the claimant` IS `I have been housed in two dwellings on account of the number of children and qualifying young persons living with me`
            `the claimant normally occupies both accommodation A and accommodation B with children or qualifying young persons for whom the claimant is responsible` IS `I normally occupy both dwellings with children or qualifying young persons I am responsible for`
            `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation A` IS `I meet the payment and liability conditions for accommodation A`
            `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of accommodation B` IS `I meet the payment and liability conditions for accommodation B`


-- Sch 3 para 5. A claimant who has moved to a new home that is being adapted for a "specified person" (the claimant, or a child or qualifying young person they are responsible for, who receives one of the listed
-- disability payments) is, if the delay in moving in was necessary and reasonable, treated as occupying both the new and the old home, but not for more than one month from the first day on which they are treated as occupying both.
@export Am I treated as occupying both my old and new home while my new home is adapted for a disabled person (Sch 3 para 5)?
GIVEN `I have moved into my new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you moved into the new accommodation?
      `immediately before the move I met the payment and liability conditions for the new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the move, did you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for the new accommodation?
      `the delay in moving in was necessary to adapt the new home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a specified person?
      `the person who needs the adaptations is me or a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whose disablement needs the adaptations you, or a child or qualifying young person for whom you are responsible?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `immediately before the move I was entitled to housing costs element for my old home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the move, were you entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in your award for the old accommodation?
      `the delay in moving in was reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the delay in moving into the new accommodation reasonable?
      `the year of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the first day on which you are treated as occupying both homes (the day you became treated as occupying both)? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the first day on which you are treated as occupying both homes (the day you became treated as occupying both)? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the first day on which you are treated as occupying both homes (the day you became treated as occupying both)? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as occupying both my old and new home while my new home is adapted` IF
    `Sch 3 para 5 — the claimant is treated as occupying both the new and the old accommodation` `my move`
    WHERE
        `my move` MEANS `Move to a new home that is adapted for a disabled person` WITH
            `the claimant has moved into the new accommodation` IS `I have moved into my new home`
            `immediately before the move, the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the new accommodation` IS `immediately before the move I met the payment and liability conditions for the new home`
            `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the new accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a specified person` IS `the delay in moving in was necessary to adapt the new home`
            `the specified person` IS `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)` WITH
                `a claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible` IS `the person who needs the adaptations is me or a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
            `immediately before the move, the claimant was entitled to the inclusion of the housing costs element in an award of universal credit in respect of the old accommodation` IS `immediately before the move I was entitled to housing costs element for my old home`
            `the delay in moving into the new accommodation was reasonable` IS `the delay in moving in was reasonable`
            `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations` IS YMD `the year of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` `the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes`
            `day to which the question relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`


-- Sch 3 para 6. A claimant who is living away from home because it is unreasonable to expect them to return, owing to a reasonable fear of violence, and who intends to return, is treated as normally
-- occupying both homes if they meet the conditions for both and it is reasonable to include an amount for both, but not for more than 12 months; otherwise the one for which they meet the conditions
-- and for which it is reasonable. After 12 months on conditions that would otherwise treat them as occupying both, the text says nothing, and the answer is the explicit "not covered" value.
@export Which home am I treated as normally occupying after leaving because of fear of violence (Sch 3 para 6)?
GIVEN `I am living in accommodation other than my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you living in accommodation other than the accommodation you normally occupy as your home?
      `it is unreasonable to expect me to return because of a reasonable fear of violence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it unreasonable to expect you to return to your home because of your reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against you or any child or qualifying young person you are responsible for?
      `I intend to return to my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you intend to return to your home?
      `I meet the payment and liability conditions for my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for your home?
      `I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for the other accommodation?
      `it is reasonable to include an amount for my home in the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it reasonable to include an amount in your housing costs element for the payments for your home?
      `it is reasonable to include an amount for the other accommodation in the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it reasonable to include an amount in your housing costs element for the payments for the other accommodation?
      `the year of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the first day on which you are treated as occupying both homes? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the first day on which you are treated as occupying both homes? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the first day on which you are treated as occupying both homes? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
GIVETH A `Accommodation treated as normally occupied under paragraph 6`
DECIDE `Which home am I treated as normally occupying after leaving because of fear of violence` IS
    `Sch 3 para 6 — the accommodation the claimant is treated as normally occupying` `my move for safety`
    WHERE
        `my move for safety` MEANS `Claimant living in other accommodation because of fear of violence` WITH
            `the claimant is occupying accommodation other than the accommodation which they normally occupy as their home` IS `I am living in accommodation other than my home`
            `it is unreasonable to expect the claimant to return to the home accommodation on account of the claimant's reasonable fear of violence in the home, or by a former partner, against the claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom the claimant is responsible` IS `it is unreasonable to expect me to return because of a reasonable fear of violence`
            `the claimant intends to return to the home accommodation` IS `I intend to return to my home`
            `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the home accommodation` IS `I meet the payment and liability conditions for my home`
            `the claimant meets the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the other accommodation` IS `I meet the payment and liability conditions for the other accommodation`
            `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the home accommodation` IS `it is reasonable to include an amount for my home in the housing costs element`
            `it is reasonable to include an amount in the housing costs element for the payments in respect of the other accommodation` IS `it is reasonable to include an amount for the other accommodation in the housing costs element`
            `first day on which the claimant is treated as occupying both accommodations` IS YMD `the year of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` `the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes` `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as occupying both homes`
            `day to which the question relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`


-- Sch 3 para 7. A claimant who moves into accommodation after a necessary and reasonable delay to adapt it for a relevant person's disablement needs is treated as having occupied it for up to one month
-- before moving in, if immediately before the move they met the payment and liability conditions.
@export Am I treated as having lived in my home before I moved in, because it was adapted for a disabled person (Sch 3 para 7)?
GIVEN `I have since moved into the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since moved into the accommodation?
      `immediately before the move I met the payment and liability conditions for the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the move, did you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for the accommodation?
      `the delay in moving in was necessary to adapt the accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was there a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person?
      `the person who needs the adaptations is me or a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whose disablement needs the adaptations you, or a child or qualifying young person for whom you are responsible?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who needs the adaptations` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `it was reasonable to delay moving in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it reasonable to delay moving in?
      `the year of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the first day on which you are treated as having occupied the accommodation? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the first day on which you are treated as having occupied the accommodation? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the first day on which you are treated as having occupied the accommodation? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having lived in my home before I moved in because it was adapted` IF
    `Sch 3 para 7 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` `my delayed move`
    WHERE
        `my delayed move` MEANS `Move that was delayed by adaptations to accommodation` WITH
            `the claimant has since moved in` IS `I have since moved into the accommodation`
            `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation` IS `immediately before the move I met the payment and liability conditions for the accommodation`
            `there was a delay in moving in that was necessary to enable the accommodation to be adapted to meet the disablement needs of a relevant person` IS `the delay in moving in was necessary to adapt the accommodation`
            `the relevant person` IS `Person who may be specified in paragraph 5(3)` WITH
                `a claimant or any child or qualifying young person for whom a claimant is responsible` IS `the person who needs the adaptations is me or a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who needs the adaptations`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who needs the adaptations`
            `it was reasonable to delay moving in` IS `it was reasonable to delay moving in`
            `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS YMD `the year of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` `the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation`
            `day to which the question relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`


-- Sch 3 para 8. A claimant who moves into accommodation following a stay in hospital or a care home is treated as having occupied it for up to one month before moving in, if the liability arose while they
-- (for joint claimants, both of them) were patients or in a care home, and immediately before the move they met the payment and liability conditions.
@export Am I treated as having lived in my home before I moved in, after a stay in hospital or a care home (Sch 3 para 8)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I have since moved in` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you since moved into the accommodation?
      `immediately before the move I met the payment and liability conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the move, did you meet the payment condition and the liability condition for the accommodation?
      `my claim basis` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Are you claiming as a single claimant, as one of joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `I was undergoing treatment as an in-patient when the liability arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the liability to make the payments arose, were you undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution?
      `I was accommodated in a care home when the liability arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the liability arose, were you accommodated in a care home?
      `the care home I was accommodated in is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where you were accommodated a care home?
      `the care home I was accommodated in is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that place an independent hospital?
      `my joint claimant was undergoing treatment as an in-patient when the liability arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the liability to make the payments arose, was your joint claimant undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in a hospital or similar institution?
      `my joint claimant was accommodated in a care home when the liability arose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc When the liability arose, was your joint claimant accommodated in a care home?
      `the care home my joint claimant was accommodated in is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the place where your joint claimant was accommodated a care home?
      `the care home my joint claimant was accommodated in is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that place an independent hospital?
      `the year of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the first day on which you are treated as having occupied the accommodation? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the first day on which you are treated as having occupied the accommodation? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the first day on which you are treated as having occupied the accommodation? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as having lived in my home before I moved in after a stay in hospital or a care home` IF
    `Sch 3 para 8 — the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation before moving in` `my move after a stay`
    WHERE
        `my move after a stay` MEANS `Move following a stay in hospital or a care home` WITH
            `the claimant has since moved in` IS `I have since moved in`
            `immediately before the move the claimant met the payment condition and the liability condition in respect of the accommodation` IS `immediately before the move I met the payment and liability conditions`
            `claim basis` IS `my claim basis`
            `the situation of the claimant when the liability to make the payments arose` IS `Person's situation when a liability arose` WITH
                `the person was undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution` IS `I was undergoing treatment as an in-patient when the liability arose`
                `the care home in which the person was accommodated` IS `uc3 seat — premises that may be a care home` `my home is in` `the care home I was accommodated in is a care home` `the care home I was accommodated in is an independent hospital`
                `the person was accommodated in that care home` IS `I was accommodated in a care home when the liability arose`
            `the situation of the other joint claimant when the liability to make the payments arose` IS `Person's situation when a liability arose` WITH
                `the person was undergoing medical or other treatment as an in-patient in any hospital or similar institution` IS `my joint claimant was undergoing treatment as an in-patient when the liability arose`
                `the care home in which the person was accommodated` IS `uc3 seat — premises that may be a care home` `my home is in` `the care home my joint claimant was accommodated in is a care home` `the care home my joint claimant was accommodated in is an independent hospital`
                `the person was accommodated in that care home` IS `my joint claimant was accommodated in a care home when the liability arose`
            `first day on which the claimant is treated as having occupied the accommodation` IS YMD `the year of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` `the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation` `the day of the month of the first day I am treated as having occupied the accommodation`
            `day to which the question relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`


-- Sch 3 para 9. A claimant is treated as no longer occupying their home if a temporary absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months; but never so if they fall within paragraph 3, and (if they fall
-- within paragraph 6) only after 12 months. A month is counted from the first day of the absence: the day that many months later is the first day that exceeds it.
@export Am I treated as no longer living in my home because of a long temporary absence (Sch 3 para 9)?
GIVEN `the year of the first day of my absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was the first day of your absence from your home? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day of my absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month was the first day of your absence from your home? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day of my absence` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the first day of your absence from your home? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the last day my absence is expected to last` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the last day to which your absence is expected to last? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the last day my absence is expected to last` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the last day to which your absence is expected to last? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the last day my absence is expected to last` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the last day to which your absence is expected to last? (1 to 31)
      `I fall within paragraph 3 of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within paragraph 3 of Schedule 3 (living elsewhere during essential repairs)?
      `I fall within paragraph 6 of Schedule 3` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within paragraph 6 of Schedule 3 (living elsewhere because of fear of violence)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I treated as no longer living in my home because of a long temporary absence` IF
    `Sch 3 para 9 — the claimant is treated as no longer occupying the accommodation` `my absence`
    WHERE
        `my absence` MEANS `Temporary absence from accommodation` WITH
            `first day of the absence` IS YMD `the year of the first day of my absence` `the month of the first day of my absence` `the day of the month of the first day of my absence`
            `day to which the question relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`
            `last day to which the absence is expected to last` IS YMD `the year of the last day my absence is expected to last` `the month of the last day my absence is expected to last` `the day of the month of the last day my absence is expected to last`
            `the claimant falls within paragraph 3` IS `I fall within paragraph 3 of Schedule 3`
            `the claimant falls within paragraph 6` IS `I fall within paragraph 6 of Schedule 3`

§§ `Schedule 4 -- housing costs element for renters`

-- Sch 4 para 4. A renter aged 16 or 17 who is a care leaver gets no housing costs element.
@export Do I get no housing costs element because I am a 16 or 17 year old care leaver (Sch 4 para 4)?
GIVEN `my age in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `I am a care leaver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a care leaver?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I get no housing costs element because I am a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` IF
    `Sch 4 para 4 — the renter gets no housing costs element as a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` `me as a renter`
    WHERE
        `me as a renter` MEANS `Renter who may be a 16 or 17 year old care leaver` WITH
            `age in complete years` IS `my age in complete years`
            `care leaver` IS `I am a care leaver`

-- Sch 4 para 6. A relevant payment is taken into account where the renter meets the payment, liability and occupation conditions for it; no payment is brought into account more than once.
-- (A service charge payment is taken to meet every paragraph 8 condition where Part 5 applies: ask the Schedule 1 question above.)
@export Is what I pay taken into account for my housing costs element (Sch 4 para 6)?
GIVEN `what I pay is a service charge payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay a service charge payment (rather than rent)?
      `my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your housing costs element worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4 (you rent from a social landlord)?
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for these payments?
      `these payments have already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have these payments already been brought into account, for you or another renter?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I pay taken into account for my housing costs element` IF
    `Sch 4 para 6 — the liability is brought into account` `what I pay`
    WHERE
        `what I pay` MEANS `uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` `what I pay is a service charge payment` `my housing costs element is worked out under Part 5 of Schedule 4` 0 `monthly payments` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` FALSE 0

-- Sch 4 para 7. A relevant payment is brought to a monthly amount: weekly payments are multiplied by 52 and divided by 12, two-weekly by 26 and divided by 12, four-weekly by 13 and divided by 12,
-- three-monthly by 4 and divided by 12, annual payments are divided by 12. If the arrangements provide for rent free periods the monthly equivalent is worked over 12 months by the number of payments
-- the renter is liable to make in those 12 months (the text's formulas for that number in paragraph 7(3A) are missing from this rendering: the number is an input).
@export What is the monthly equivalent of what I pay (Sch 4 para 7)?
GIVEN `the amount of each payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each payment, in pounds?
      `how often the payment falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the payment fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my arrangements provide for rent free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements provide for one or more rent free periods (or service charge free periods)?
      `the total number of payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many payments are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the monthly equivalent of what I pay` IS
    `Sch 4 para 7 — the monthly equivalent of an amount` `the amount of each payment` `how often the payment falls due` `my arrangements provide for rent free periods` `the total number of payments in the 12 month period`

-- Sch 4 para 9. A person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit if they are the renter (or a joint renter), a child or qualifying young person the renter is responsible for, or a non-dependant: a person who
-- normally lives in the accommodation with the renter and is none of the following: a renter, child or qualifying young person (paragraph 9(1)(a) or (b)); the other member of a couple claiming as a single person;
-- a foster child; a person liable to pay the renter on a commercial basis; the person the liability is owed to (or their household); a person already treated as a non-dependant for another person's claim;
-- or a child or qualifying young person nobody in the unit is responsible for.
@export Is this person a member of my extended benefit unit (Sch 4 para 9)?
GIVEN `the person is me, or one of my joint renters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person you are asking about you, or one of your joint renters?
      `the person is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a child or qualifying young person for whom you (or either joint renter) are responsible?
      `the person is a renter or a child or qualifying young person, as paragraph 9(1)(a) or (b) says` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a renter, or a child or qualifying young person for whom a renter is responsible (paragraph 9(1)(a) or (b))?
      `the person normally lives in my accommodation with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person normally live in the accommodation with you (or with you and your joint renters)?
      `the person is the other member of a couple who is claiming as a single person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Where you are a member of a couple claiming as a single person, is the person the other member of the couple?
      `the person is a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a child?
      `the nation in which the child is placed with me` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc If the person is a child placed with you, in which nation of Great Britain is the child placed?
      `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the child placed with you under the placement regulations?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a foster carer or a kinship carer?
      `the person is liable to make payments to me on a commercial basis for living in my accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of their occupation of the accommodation?
      `the person is owed the liability to make relevant payments or is a member of that person's household` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed, or a member of their household?
      `the person has already been treated as a non-dependant for another person's claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the person already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments for the accommodation?
      `the person is a child or qualifying young person nobody in my extended benefit unit is responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in your extended benefit unit is responsible?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person a member of my extended benefit unit` IF
    `Sch 4 para 9(1) — a person is a member of the renter's extended benefit unit` `this person`
    WHERE
        `this person` MEANS `Person who may be a member of an extended benefit unit` WITH
            `the renter (or one of joint renters)` IS `the person is me, or one of my joint renters`
            `a child or qualifying young person for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible` IS `the person is a child or qualifying young person I am responsible for`
            `the person as a possible non-dependant` IS `Person who may be a non-dependant` WITH
                `normally lives in the accommodation with the renter (or joint renters)` IS `the person normally lives in my accommodation with me`
                `a person within sub-paragraph (1)(a) or (b)` IS `the person is a renter or a child or qualifying young person, as paragraph 9(1)(a) or (b) says`
                `where the renter is a member of a couple claiming as a single person, the other member of the couple` IS `the person is the other member of a couple who is claiming as a single person`
                `the person as a possible foster child` IS `Child who may be a foster child` WITH
                    child IS `the person is a child`
                    `the child's placement with the renter (or either joint renter)` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                        `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation in which the child is placed with me`
                        `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `the child is placed with me under the placement regulations`
                        `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
                `a person who is liable to make payments on a commercial basis in respect of the person's occupation of the accommodation` IS `the person is liable to make payments to me on a commercial basis for living in my accommodation`
                `a person to whom the liability to make relevant payments is owed or a member of their household` IS `the person is owed the liability to make relevant payments or is a member of that person's household`
                `a person who has already been treated as a non-dependant in relation to a claim for universal credit by another person liable to make relevant payments in respect of the accommodation occupied by the renter` IS `the person has already been treated as a non-dependant for another person's claim`
                `a child or qualifying young person for whom no-one in the renter's extended benefit unit is responsible` IS `the person is a child or qualifying young person nobody in my extended benefit unit is responsible for`

-- Sch 4 para 10 (with paras 11 and 12). A renter in the social rented sector is entitled to one bedroom, and one more for each qualifying young person, each non-dependant who is not a child, and the fewest
-- bedrooms the children can be fitted into if each child under 10, and each pair of the same sex, shares; plus an additional bedroom for each of: a person who needs overnight care, a foster parent (or a
-- person who would be one, or an adopter), a child who cannot share because of disability, and a renter who cannot share with a joint renter. Children are counted by age and sex, and the
-- seat takes at most one person for the overnight care condition, one foster parent, and one renter who cannot share (the layer-1 rule takes any number).
@export How many bedrooms am I entitled to (Sch 4 paras 10 to 12)?
GIVEN `the number of qualifying young persons I am responsible for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying young persons are you (or you and your partner) responsible for?
      `the number of non-dependants in my household who are not children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many non-dependants live with you who are not children?
      `the number of boys under 10 in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many boys under 10 years old are in your extended benefit unit?
      `the number of girls under 10 in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many girls under 10 years old are in your extended benefit unit?
      `the number of boys aged 10 or over in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many boys aged 10 or over are in your extended benefit unit?
      `the number of girls aged 10 or over in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many girls aged 10 or over are in your extended benefit unit?
      `of those, the number of boys under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the boys under 10, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `of those, the number of girls under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the girls under 10, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `of those, the number of boys aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the boys aged 10 or over, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `of those, the number of girls aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the girls aged 10 or over, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `one or more people who do not live in my home are engaged to provide overnight care and to stay overnight on a regular basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are one or more people who do not live in your home engaged to provide overnight care for that person and to stay overnight in your home on a regular basis?
      `the overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the overnight care provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose?
      `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child placed with you under the placement regulations?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a foster carer or a kinship carer?
      `the nation in which the child is placed` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be a foster parent but for the fact that you do not currently have any child placed with you?
      `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption?
      `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `I would be expected to share a bedroom with my joint renter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the provisions on additional bedrooms, would you be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter?
      `I am not reasonably able to share a bedroom with my joint renter because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of your disability, are you not reasonably able to share a bedroom with your joint renter?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many bedrooms am I entitled to` IS
    `Sch 4 para 10 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria` WITH
            `qualifying young persons for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible` IS `the number of qualifying young persons I am responsible for`
            `non-dependants who are not children` IS `the number of non-dependants in my household who are not children`
            children IS `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
                `male children under 10 years old` IS `the number of boys under 10 in my household`
                `female children under 10 years old` IS `the number of girls under 10 in my household`
                `male children aged 10 or over` IS `the number of boys aged 10 or over in my household`
                `female children aged 10 or over` IS `the number of girls aged 10 or over in my household`
            `disabled children` IS `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
                `male children under 10 years old` IS `of those, the number of boys under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `female children under 10 years old` IS `of those, the number of girls under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `male children aged 10 or over` IS `of those, the number of boys aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `female children aged 10 or over` IS `of those, the number of girls aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability`
            `persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition` IS LIST `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition` WITH
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                `one or more persons who do not live in the renter's accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis` IS `one or more people who do not live in my home are engaged to provide overnight care and to stay overnight on a regular basis`
                `overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS `the overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose`
            `renters as holders of the foster parent condition` IS LIST `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` WITH
                    `the renter's placement of a child` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                        `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation in which the child is placed`
                        `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations`
                        `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
                    `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them` IS `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now`
                    `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent` IS YMD `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved`
                    `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care`
                    `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption` IS `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption`
            `renters as holders of the disabled person condition` IS LIST `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition` WITH
                `the renter would, but for the provisions of this paragraph, be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter` IS `I would be expected to share a bedroom with my joint renter`
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the disabled renter`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the disabled renter`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the disabled renter`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the disabled renter`
                `by virtue of their disability, the renter is not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter` IS `I am not reasonably able to share a bedroom with my joint renter because of my disability`

-- Sch 4 para 11(2). A child or qualifying young person who is temporarily absent is still counted in the extended benefit unit for the first 6 months of an absence in the care of a local authority (if they were in
-- the unit, and the award included the housing costs element, immediately before), for the first 6 months of an absence as a prisoner on the same terms and without a longer sentence expected, or before
-- responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7).
@export Is my temporarily absent child or qualifying young person still counted in my extended benefit unit (Sch 4 para 11)?
GIVEN `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was the first day of the absence? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month was the first day of the absence? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the first day of the absence? (1 to 31)
      `I am treated as not responsible for the child or qualifying young person under regulation 4(6)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person because a local authority looks after them (regulation 4(6)(a))?
      `immediately before the local authority started looking after them the child was in my extended benefit unit and my award included the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the local authority started looking after them, was the child or qualifying young person included in your extended benefit unit and did your award include the housing costs element?
      `I am treated as not responsible for the child or qualifying young person under regulation 4(6)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person because they are a prisoner (regulation 4(6)(b))?
      `immediately before becoming a prisoner the child was in my extended benefit unit and my award included the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before becoming a prisoner, was the child or qualifying young person included in your extended benefit unit and did your award include the housing costs element?
      `the child has not been sentenced to a term in custody expected to extend beyond 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the child or qualifying young person not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond the 6 months?
      `the day I am asking about is before my responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the day you are asking about fall before you cease to be responsible for the temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my temporarily absent child or qualifying young person still counted in my extended benefit unit` IF
    `Sch 4 para 11(2) — a temporarily absent child or qualifying young person is included` `the absent child`
    WHERE
        `the absent child` MEANS `Temporarily absent child or qualifying young person` WITH
            `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`
            `first day of the absence` IS YMD `the year of the first day of the absence` `the month of the first day of the absence` `the day of the month of the first day of the absence`
            `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(a)` IS `I am treated as not responsible for the child or qualifying young person under regulation 4(6)(a)`
            `immediately before the local authority started looking after them the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element` IS `immediately before the local authority started looking after them the child was in my extended benefit unit and my award included the housing costs element`
            `the renter is treated as not being responsible for the child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(6)(b)` IS `I am treated as not responsible for the child or qualifying young person under regulation 4(6)(b)`
            `immediately before becoming a prisoner the child or qualifying young person was included in the renter's extended benefit unit and the renter's award included the housing costs element` IS `immediately before becoming a prisoner the child was in my extended benefit unit and my award included the housing costs element`
            `the child or qualifying young person has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months` IS `the child has not been sentenced to a term in custody expected to extend beyond 6 months`
            `the determination relates to a time before the renter or joint renter ceases to be responsible for the temporarily absent child or qualifying young person in accordance with regulation 4(7)` IS `the day I am asking about is before my responsibility ceases under regulation 4(7)`

-- Sch 4 para 11(3). A renter who is temporarily absent is still counted if their temporary absence from Great Britain is disregarded under regulation 11(1) or (2), or they are a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies.
@export Am I still counted as a renter while I am temporarily away (Sch 4 para 11)?
GIVEN `my temporary absence from Great Britain is disregarded under regulation 11(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your temporary absence from Great Britain disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)?
      `I am a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still counted as a renter while I am temporarily away` IF
    `Sch 4 para 11(3) — a temporarily absent renter is included` `my absence`
    WHERE
        `my absence` MEANS `Temporarily absent renter` WITH
            `the temporary absence from Great Britain of the renter is disregarded in accordance with regulation 11(1) or (2)` IS `my temporary absence from Great Britain is disregarded under regulation 11(1) or (2)`
            `the renter is a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies` IS `I am a prisoner to whom regulation 19(2) applies`

-- Sch 4 para 11(4) and (5). A temporarily absent non-dependant (who was in the unit immediately before) is still counted: for the first month of an absence from Great Britain (two months where the circumstances would
-- be disregarded for regulation 11(2)), for the first 6 months of an absence for treatment or as a prisoner without a longer sentence expected (if the award included the housing costs element), or without limit for a son or
-- daughter in the armed forces away on operations.
@export Is my temporarily absent non-dependant still counted in my extended benefit unit (Sch 4 para 11)?
GIVEN `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was the first day of the absence? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month was the first day of the absence? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the first day of the absence? (1 to 31)
      `the absence is a temporary absence from Great Britain` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence a temporary absence from Great Britain?
      `the non-dependant's circumstances would be disregarded for regulation 11(2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the circumstances of the non-dependant such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2)?
      `the absence from Great Britain is in the circumstances of regulation 11(3)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence from Great Britain in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a) (treatment)?
      `the non-dependant is a prisoner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the non-dependant a prisoner?
      `the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody expected to extend beyond 6 months` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the non-dependant not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond the 6 months?
      `the non-dependant is my son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the non-dependant the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of you or your joint renters?
      `the non-dependant is a member of the armed forces away on operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the non-dependant a member of the armed forces away on operations?
      `immediately before the period the non-dependant was in my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the start of the period, was the non-dependant included in your extended benefit unit?
      `immediately before the period my award included the housing costs element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Immediately before the start of the period, did your award include the housing costs element?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my temporarily absent non-dependant still counted in my extended benefit unit` IF
    `Sch 4 para 11(4) — a temporarily absent non-dependant is included` `the absent non-dependant`
    WHERE
        `the absent non-dependant` MEANS `Temporarily absent non-dependant` WITH
            `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about` `the month of the day I am asking about` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about`
            `first day of the absence` IS YMD `the year of the first day of the absence` `the month of the first day of the absence` `the day of the month of the first day of the absence`
            `the absence is a temporary absence from Great Britain` IS `the absence is a temporary absence from Great Britain`
            `the circumstances of the non-dependant are such as would be disregarded for the purposes of regulation 11(2)` IS `the non-dependant's circumstances would be disregarded for regulation 11(2)`
            `the absence from Great Britain is in the circumstances described in regulation 11(3)(a)` IS `the absence from Great Britain is in the circumstances of regulation 11(3)(a)`
            `the non-dependant is a prisoner` IS `the non-dependant is a prisoner`
            `the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody that is expected to extend beyond that 6 months` IS `the non-dependant has not been sentenced to a term in custody expected to extend beyond 6 months`
            `the non-dependant is the son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter of a renter or joint renters` IS `the non-dependant is my son, daughter, step-son or step-daughter`
            `the non-dependant is a member of the armed forces away on operations` IS `the non-dependant is a member of the armed forces away on operations`
            `immediately before the start of the period the non-dependant was included in the renter's extended benefit unit` IS `immediately before the period the non-dependant was in my extended benefit unit`
            `immediately before the start of the period the renter's award included the housing costs element` IS `immediately before the period my award included the housing costs element`

-- Sch 4 para 11(6). A non-dependant who is absent in other circumstances is not treated as a member of the extended benefit unit if the absence exceeds, or is expected to exceed, 6 months. (A month is counted from the first day.)
@export Is my absent non-dependant no longer counted in my extended benefit unit because of a long absence (Sch 4 para 11)?
GIVEN `the year of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was the first day of the absence? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month was the first day of the absence? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day of the absence` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the first day of the absence? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the last day the absence is expected to last` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the last day to which the absence is expected to last? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the last day the absence is expected to last` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the last day to which the absence is expected to last? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the last day the absence is expected to last` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the last day to which the absence is expected to last? (1 to 31)
      `the absence is in circumstances other than those in paragraphs 11(4) and (5)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the absence in circumstances other than those specified in sub-paragraphs (4) and (5)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
