-- Sch 4 para 17. A renter treated as occupying a single accommodation under Schedule 3 paragraph 4 (two dwellings, A and B) has one calculation made for both: under Part 5 where the rent for A and for B
-- is payable to a provider of social housing, and under Part 4 in any other case; the bedrooms in A and B count together, and so do the relevant payments for both.
@export Under which Part of Schedule 4 is my housing costs element worked out if I am housed in two dwellings (Sch 4 para 17)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
