      `the landlord of dwelling A is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling A a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `the landlord of dwelling A is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling A a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `dwelling A is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is dwelling A social housing?
      `the landlord of dwelling A is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling A a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `the landlord of dwelling B is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling B a local authority?
      `the landlord of dwelling B is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling B a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `the landlord of dwelling B is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling B a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `dwelling B is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is dwelling B social housing?
      `the landlord of dwelling B is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the landlord of dwelling B a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
GIVETH A `Part of Schedule 4 under which the housing costs element is calculated`
DECIDE `Under which Part of Schedule 4 is my housing costs element worked out if I am housed in two dwellings` IS
    `Sch 4 para 17(3) and (4) — the Part under which the single calculation is made` `my two dwellings`
    WHERE
        `my two dwellings` MEANS `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation` WITH
            `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation A are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` `my home is in` `the landlord of dwelling A is a local authority` `the landlord of dwelling A is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the landlord of dwelling A is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `dwelling A is social housing` `the landlord of dwelling A is a registered social landlord`
            `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation B are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` `my home is in` `the landlord of dwelling B is a local authority` `the landlord of dwelling B is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the landlord of dwelling B is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `dwelling B is social housing` `the landlord of dwelling B is a registered social landlord`
            `number of bedrooms in accommodation A` IS 0
            `number of bedrooms in accommodation B` IS 0
            `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation A` IS EMPTY
            `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation B` IS EMPTY

@export How many bedrooms count if I am housed in two dwellings (Sch 4 para 17)?
GIVEN `the number of bedrooms in dwelling A` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are there in dwelling A?
      `the number of bedrooms in dwelling B` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are there in dwelling B?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many bedrooms count if I am housed in two dwellings` IS
    `Sch 4 para 17(2)(b) — the total number of bedrooms in accommodation A and accommodation B taken together` `my two dwellings`
    WHERE
        `my two dwellings` MEANS `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation` WITH
            `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation A are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that is not a provider of social housing`
            `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation B are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that is not a provider of social housing`
            `number of bedrooms in accommodation A` IS `the number of bedrooms in dwelling A`
            `number of bedrooms in accommodation B` IS `the number of bedrooms in dwelling B`
            `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation A` IS EMPTY
            `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation B` IS EMPTY

@export What is the monthly total of what I pay for my two dwellings (Sch 4 para 17)?
GIVEN `the amount of each dwelling A rent payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each rent payment for dwelling A, in pounds?
      `how often the dwelling A rent falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the rent for dwelling A fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my dwelling A rent arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for the rent for dwelling A provide for one or more rent free periods?
      `the total number of dwelling A rent payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many rent payments for dwelling A are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `the amount of each dwelling B rent payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each rent payment for dwelling B, in pounds?
      `how often the dwelling B rent falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the rent for dwelling B fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my dwelling B rent arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for the rent for dwelling B provide for one or more rent free periods?
      `the total number of dwelling B rent payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many rent payments for dwelling B are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for these payments?
      `these payments have already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have these payments already been brought into account, for you or another renter?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the monthly total of what I pay for my two dwellings` IS
    `Sch 4 para 17(2)(a) — the monthly amount of all the relevant payments in respect of accommodation A and accommodation B` `my two dwellings`
    WHERE
        `my two dwellings` MEANS `Renter treated as occupying a single accommodation` WITH
            `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation A are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that is not a provider of social housing`
            `the landlord that rent payments in respect of accommodation B are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that is not a provider of social housing`
            `number of bedrooms in accommodation A` IS 0
            `number of bedrooms in accommodation B` IS 0
            `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation A` IS LIST `uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` FALSE FALSE `the amount of each dwelling A rent payment` `how often the dwelling A rent falls due` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` `my dwelling A rent arrangements provide for free periods` `the total number of dwelling A rent payments in the 12 month period`
            `liabilities for payments in respect of accommodation B` IS LIST `uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` FALSE FALSE `the amount of each dwelling B rent payment` `how often the dwelling B rent falls due` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` `my dwelling B rent arrangements provide for free periods` `the total number of dwelling B rent payments in the 12 month period`

-- Sch 4 para 18. For a renter treated (Sch 3 para 5) as occupying both the new and the old home while the new home is adapted for a disabled person, the housing costs element is the sum of the amounts for the two homes,
-- and where a deduction for housing cost contributions was made for both, the contributions deducted for the new home are added back.
@export What is my housing costs element while I am treated as occupying my new and old home (Sch 4 para 18)?
GIVEN `the amount of my housing costs element for the new home` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your housing costs element for the new accommodation worked out under Part 4 or Part 5, in pounds?
      `the amount of my housing costs element for the old home` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your housing costs element for the old accommodation worked out under Part 4 or Part 5, in pounds?
      `a deduction for housing cost contributions was made for both the new and the old home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a deduction for housing cost contributions made in respect of both the new accommodation and the old accommodation?
      `the housing cost contributions deducted for the new home` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of housing cost contributions was deducted in respect of the new accommodation, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my housing costs element while I am treated as occupying my new and old home` IS
    `Sch 4 para 18(2) — the amount of the renter's housing costs element` `the amount of my housing costs element for the new home` `the amount of my housing costs element for the old home` `a deduction for housing cost contributions was made for both the new and the old home` `the housing cost contributions deducted for the new home`

-- Sch 4 para 19. For a renter who has left home because of a reasonable fear of violence and is treated (Sch 3 para 6(2)) as occupying both the home and the other accommodation, the housing costs element is the sum
-- of the amounts for both, and where a deduction for housing cost contributions was made for both, the contributions deducted for the accommodation the renter does not normally occupy as their home are added back.
@export What is my housing costs element while I am treated as occupying both my home and the place I fled to (Sch 4 para 19)?
GIVEN `the amount of my housing costs element for my home accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your housing costs element for the accommodation you normally occupy as your home, worked out under Part 4 or Part 5, in pounds?
      `the amount of my housing costs element for the other accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of your housing costs element for the other accommodation, worked out under Part 4 or Part 5, in pounds?
      `a deduction for housing cost contributions was made for both my home and the other accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a deduction for housing cost contributions made in respect of both?
      `the housing cost contributions deducted for my home accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of housing cost contributions was deducted in respect of the accommodation you normally occupy as your home, in pounds?
      `the housing cost contributions deducted for the other accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What amount of housing cost contributions was deducted in respect of the other accommodation, in pounds?
      `the accommodation I normally occupy as my home` IS A `Accommodation the renter normally occupies as their home` @desc Which accommodation do you normally occupy as your home? (the home accommodation or the other accommodation)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my housing costs element while I am treated as occupying both my home and the place I fled to` IS
    `Sch 4 para 19(2) — the amount of the renter's housing costs element` `the amount of my housing costs element for my home accommodation` `the amount of my housing costs element for the other accommodation` `a deduction for housing cost contributions was made for both my home and the other accommodation` `the housing cost contributions deducted for my home accommodation` `the housing cost contributions deducted for the other accommodation` `the accommodation I normally occupy as my home`

