    `Sch 4 para 20 — Part 4 applies to the renter` `my renting`
    WHERE
        `my renting` MEANS `Renter whose landlord decides the Part` WITH
            `the landlord that rent payments are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` `my home is in` `my landlord is a local authority` `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `my home is social housing` `my landlord is a registered social landlord`
            `the renter is also liable to make service charge payments` IS `I am also liable to make service charge payments`

-- Sch 4 paras 22 to 25. Under Part 4 (the private rented sector) the housing costs element is the lower of the core rent and the cap rent, less the housing cost contributions. The core rent is the monthly total of
-- the relevant payments taken into account; where others are liable with the renter it is the allocated share. These questions take it that what you pay is rent and, if you pay one, a service charge payment.
@export What is my housing costs element if I rent privately (Sch 4 paras 22 to 25)?
GIVEN `the amount of each rent payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each rent payment, in pounds? (0 if there is none)
      `how often the rent falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the rent fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my rent arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for the rent provide for one or more periods in which it is not payable?
      `the total number of rent payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many rent payments are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `the amount of each service charge payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each service charge payment, in pounds? (0 if there is none)
      `how often the service charge falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the service charge fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my service charge arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for the service charge provide for one or more periods in which it is not payable?
      `the total number of service charge payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many service charge payments are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for these payments?
      `these payments have already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have these payments already been brought into account, for you or another renter?
      `the number of listed persons liable for the payments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the people liable to make the payments are you, your partner, or a child or qualifying young person you are responsible for? (the listed persons)
      `the number of other persons liable for the payments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other people are liable to make the payments with you?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that sharing the payments by number of people would be unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it would be unreasonable to share the payments according to the number of people liable?
      `the amount the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what amount does the Secretary of State consider appropriate in all the circumstances, in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the local housing allowance for the broad rental market area in which your accommodation is situated and the category of accommodation you are entitled to, in pounds a month?
      `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 apply to you (housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing)?
      `the local housing allowance for accommodation A` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the local housing allowance for accommodation A, in pounds a month? (0 if not applicable)
      `the local housing allowance for accommodation B` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the local housing allowance for accommodation B, in pounds a month? (0 if not applicable)
      `a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a single calculation made for you under paragraph 17 for both dwellings?
      `this is the first calculation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first calculation?
      `I have been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined?
      `the accommodation for which the allowance was lower when the calculation was first made` IS A `Accommodation for the cap rent` @desc For which dwelling was the allowance lower when the calculation was first made? (accommodation A or accommodation B)
      `the housing cost contributions to be deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum of the housing cost contributions to be deducted, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my housing costs element if I rent privately` IS
    `Sch 4 para 22 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 4` `my core rent` `my cap rent` `the housing cost contributions to be deducted`
    WHERE
        `my core rent` MEANS `Sch 4 para 24 — core rent for joint tenants` `our joint liability`
        `our joint liability` MEANS `Joint liability for relevant payments` WITH
            `liabilities of the renter and of the others for relevant payments in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole` IS LIST `uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` FALSE FALSE `the amount of each rent payment` `how often the rent falls due` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` `my rent arrangements provide for free periods` `the total number of rent payments in the 12 month period`, `uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` TRUE FALSE `the amount of each service charge payment` `how often the service charge falls due` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` `my service charge arrangements provide for free periods` `the total number of service charge payments in the 12 month period`
            `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments` IS `the number of listed persons liable for the payments`
            `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments` IS `the number of other persons liable for the payments`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to allocate the amount in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied that sharing the payments by number of people would be unreasonable`
            `the amount allocated in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances` IS `the amount the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        `my cap rent` MEANS `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` `my cap rent facts`
        `my cap rent facts` MEANS `Facts for the cap rent` WITH
            `local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation` IS `the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation`
            `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter` IS `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me`
            `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A` IS `the local housing allowance for accommodation A`
            `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B` IS `the local housing allowance for accommodation B`
            `a single calculation is made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17` IS `a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17`
            `this is the first calculation` IS `this is the first calculation`
            `the renter has been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined` IS `I have been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined`
            `the accommodation for which the amount was lower when the calculation was first made` IS `the accommodation for which the allowance was lower when the calculation was first made`

-- Sch 4 para 25. The cap rent is the local housing allowance for the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation the renter is entitled to. Where paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies, the allowances for
-- the two dwellings differ and a single calculation is made under paragraph 17, it is the allowance of the dwelling for which it was lower when the calculation was first made, until the renter is re-housed.
@export What is my cap rent (Sch 4 para 25)?
GIVEN `the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the local housing allowance for the broad rental market area in which your accommodation is situated and the category of accommodation you are entitled to, in pounds a month?
      `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 apply to you (housed in two dwellings by a provider of social housing)?
      `the local housing allowance for accommodation A` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the local housing allowance for accommodation A, in pounds a month? (0 if not applicable)
      `the local housing allowance for accommodation B` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the local housing allowance for accommodation B, in pounds a month? (0 if not applicable)
      `a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a single calculation made for you under paragraph 17 for both dwellings?
      `this is the first calculation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is this the first calculation?
      `I have been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined?
      `the accommodation for which the allowance was lower when the calculation was first made` IS A `Accommodation for the cap rent` @desc For which dwelling was the allowance lower when the calculation was first made? (accommodation A or accommodation B)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my cap rent` IS
    `Sch 4 para 25 — cap rent` `my cap rent facts`
    WHERE
        `my cap rent facts` MEANS `Facts for the cap rent` WITH
            `local housing allowance which applies at the relevant time to the broad rental market area and the category of accommodation` IS `the local housing allowance for my area and category of accommodation`
            `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to the renter` IS `paragraph 4 of Schedule 3 applies to me`
            `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation A` IS `the local housing allowance for accommodation A`
            `local housing allowance determined under sub-paragraph (2) in relation to accommodation B` IS `the local housing allowance for accommodation B`
            `a single calculation is made in relation to the renter under paragraph 17` IS `a single calculation is made for me under paragraph 17`
            `this is the first calculation` IS `this is the first calculation`
            `the renter has been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined` IS `I have been re-housed in other accommodation since the amount was last determined`
            `the accommodation for which the amount was lower when the calculation was first made` IS `the accommodation for which the allowance was lower when the calculation was first made`

-- Sch 4 para 26. For a renter in the private rented sector the entitlement of paragraph 10 is limited to 4 bedrooms.
@export How many bedrooms am I entitled to in the private rented sector (Sch 4 para 26)?
GIVEN `the number of qualifying young persons I am responsible for` IS A NUMBER @desc How many qualifying young persons are you (or you and your partner) responsible for?
      `the number of non-dependants in my household who are not children` IS A NUMBER @desc How many non-dependants live with you who are not children?
      `the number of boys under 10 in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many boys under 10 years old are in your extended benefit unit?
      `the number of girls under 10 in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many girls under 10 years old are in your extended benefit unit?
      `the number of boys aged 10 or over in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many boys aged 10 or over are in your extended benefit unit?
      `the number of girls aged 10 or over in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many girls aged 10 or over are in your extended benefit unit?
      `of those, the number of boys under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the boys under 10, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `of those, the number of girls under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the girls under 10, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `of those, the number of boys aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the boys aged 10 or over, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `of those, the number of girls aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability` IS A NUMBER @desc Of the girls aged 10 or over, how many receive one of the listed care components and, because of their disability, are not reasonably able to share a room with another child?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `one or more people who do not live in my home are engaged to provide overnight care and to stay overnight on a regular basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are one or more people who do not live in your home engaged to provide overnight care for that person and to stay overnight in your home on a regular basis?
      `the overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the overnight care provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose?
      `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child placed with you under the placement regulations?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a foster carer or a kinship carer?
      `the nation in which the child is placed` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be a foster parent but for the fact that you do not currently have any child placed with you?
      `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption?
      `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `I would be expected to share a bedroom with my joint renter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the provisions on additional bedrooms, would you be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter?
      `I am not reasonably able to share a bedroom with my joint renter because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of your disability, are you not reasonably able to share a bedroom with your joint renter?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many bedrooms am I entitled to in the private rented sector` IS
    `Sch 4 para 26 — the number of bedrooms to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria` WITH
            `qualifying young persons for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible` IS `the number of qualifying young persons I am responsible for`
            `non-dependants who are not children` IS `the number of non-dependants in my household who are not children`
            children IS `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
                `male children under 10 years old` IS `the number of boys under 10 in my household`
                `female children under 10 years old` IS `the number of girls under 10 in my household`
                `male children aged 10 or over` IS `the number of boys aged 10 or over in my household`
                `female children aged 10 or over` IS `the number of girls aged 10 or over in my household`
            `disabled children` IS `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
                `male children under 10 years old` IS `of those, the number of boys under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `female children under 10 years old` IS `of those, the number of girls under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `male children aged 10 or over` IS `of those, the number of boys aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `female children aged 10 or over` IS `of those, the number of girls aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability`
            `persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition` IS LIST `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition` WITH
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                `one or more persons who do not live in the renter's accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis` IS `one or more people who do not live in my home are engaged to provide overnight care and to stay overnight on a regular basis`
                `overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS `the overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose`
            `renters as holders of the foster parent condition` IS LIST `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` WITH
                    `the renter's placement of a child` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                        `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation in which the child is placed`
                        `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations`
                        `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
                    `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them` IS `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now`
                    `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent` IS YMD `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved`
                    `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care`
                    `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption` IS `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption`
            `renters as holders of the disabled person condition` IS LIST `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition` WITH
                `the renter would, but for the provisions of this paragraph, be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter` IS `I would be expected to share a bedroom with my joint renter`
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the disabled renter`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the disabled renter`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the disabled renter`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the disabled renter`
                `by virtue of their disability, the renter is not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter` IS `I am not reasonably able to share a bedroom with my joint renter because of my disability`

