      `pension age disability payment, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who has an overnight carer` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does that person receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `one or more people who do not live in my home are engaged to provide overnight care and to stay overnight on a regular basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are one or more people who do not live in your home engaged to provide overnight care for that person and to stay overnight in your home on a regular basis?
      `the overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the overnight care provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose?
      `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child placed with you under the placement regulations?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a foster carer or a kinship carer?
      `the nation in which the child is placed` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be a foster parent but for the fact that you do not currently have any child placed with you?
      `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption?
      `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `I would be expected to share a bedroom with my joint renter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc But for the provisions on additional bedrooms, would you be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter?
      `I am not reasonably able to share a bedroom with my joint renter because of my disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Because of your disability, are you not reasonably able to share a bedroom with your joint renter?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the disabled renter` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: does the renter who cannot share a bedroom receive it, are they entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
GIVETH A `Category of accommodation`
DECIDE `What category of accommodation am I entitled to in the private rented sector` IS
    `Sch 4 para 27(1) — the category of accommodation to which a renter is entitled under Part 4` `I am a specified renter` `my household`
    WHERE
        `my household` MEANS `Extended benefit unit for the size criteria` WITH
            `qualifying young persons for whom the renter or either joint renter is responsible` IS `the number of qualifying young persons I am responsible for`
            `non-dependants who are not children` IS `the number of non-dependants in my household who are not children`
            children IS `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
                `male children under 10 years old` IS `the number of boys under 10 in my household`
                `female children under 10 years old` IS `the number of girls under 10 in my household`
                `male children aged 10 or over` IS `the number of boys aged 10 or over in my household`
                `female children aged 10 or over` IS `the number of girls aged 10 or over in my household`
            `disabled children` IS `Children in a renter's extended benefit unit` WITH
                `male children under 10 years old` IS `of those, the number of boys under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `female children under 10 years old` IS `of those, the number of girls under 10 who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `male children aged 10 or over` IS `of those, the number of boys aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability`
                `female children aged 10 or over` IS `of those, the number of girls aged 10 or over who cannot share a room because of disability`
            `persons who may satisfy the overnight care condition` IS LIST `Person who may satisfy the overnight care condition` WITH
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the person who has an overnight carer`
                `one or more persons who do not live in the renter's accommodation are engaged to provide overnight care for the person and to stay overnight in the accommodation on a regular basis` IS `one or more people who do not live in my home are engaged to provide overnight care and to stay overnight on a regular basis`
                `overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose` IS `the overnight care is provided under arrangements entered into for that purpose`
            `renters as holders of the foster parent condition` IS LIST `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` WITH
                    `the renter's placement of a child` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                        `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation in which the child is placed`
                        `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations`
                        `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
                    `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them` IS `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now`
                    `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent` IS YMD `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved`
                    `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care`
                    `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption` IS `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption`
            `renters as holders of the disabled person condition` IS LIST `Renter who may satisfy the disabled person condition` WITH
                `the renter would, but for the provisions of this paragraph, be expected to share a bedroom with a joint renter` IS `I would be expected to share a bedroom with my joint renter`
                payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                    `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for the disabled renter`
                    `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for the disabled renter`
                    `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for the disabled renter`
                    `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for the disabled renter`
                    `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for the disabled renter`
                `by virtue of their disability, the renter is not reasonably able to share a bedroom with the joint renter` IS `I am not reasonably able to share a bedroom with my joint renter because of my disability`

-- Sch 4 para 28. A renter is a "specified renter" if they are a single person (or a member of a couple claiming as a single person) who is under 35 and is not an excepted person, who is not responsible for any
-- children or qualifying young persons, and in relation to whom no person is a non-dependant.
@export Am I a specified renter (Sch 4 para 28)?
GIVEN `my age in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18?
      `the building has accommodation that is not self-contained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building one where domestic accommodation is provided for people generally, or for a class of people, otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises?
      `the building provides board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide board?
      `the building provides facilities for preparing food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide facilities for preparing food adequate to the needs of those people?
      `the building is owned or managed by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building owned or managed by a local authority?
      `the building is owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `the building is owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `the building is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building social housing?
      `the building is owned or managed by a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `the building is not run on a commercial basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building operated other than on a commercial basis?
      `the building is funded by government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are funds for the building provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority?
      `the building's manager is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manager of the building a public authority?
      `the building's manager is not run for profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the manager of the building carry on its activities otherwise than for profit?
      `the building's manager is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manager of the building a registered charity?
      `the building helps residents to be resettled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide care, support or supervision with a view to helping the people there to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the building is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building a care home?
      `the building is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building an independent hospital?
      `the main purpose of the hostel is accommodation with care, support or supervision for homeless people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the main purpose of that building to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to helping them to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the number of months I lived in that hostel` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months have you lived in hostels of that kind? (add together all your stays)
      `while living in the hostel I was offered and accepted services to help me be resettled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While you lived there, were you offered and did you accept services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to help you to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `I am subject to active multi-agency management under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to active multi-agency management under arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003?
      `I am subject to active multi-agency risk management under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to active multi-agency risk management under arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the Management of Offenders etc. (Scotland) Act 2005?
      `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(b) or (d) is not fully in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 10(1) of the 2005 Act not apply to you only because section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force?
      `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(e) is not fully in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 10(1) of the 2005 Act not apply to you only because section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force?
      `the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider you a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large?
      `by reason of an offence I have been convicted of, the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of an offence of which you have been convicted, does the Secretary of State consider you a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large?
      `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child placed with you under the placement regulations?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a foster carer or a kinship carer?
      `the nation in which the child is placed` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be a foster parent but for the fact that you do not currently have any child placed with you?
      `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption?
      `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `after attaining the age of 16 I had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After attaining the age of 16, did your partner or former partner, or a relative, inflict domestic violence upon you or threaten you with it?
      `the person who gave evidence is a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person who gave evidence is a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a police officer?
      `the person who gave evidence is a registered social worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person who gave evidence is the victim's employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened the victim's employer?
      `the person who gave evidence is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence?
      `my circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your circumstances consistent with your having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against you?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a police officer?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a registered social worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is the victim's employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident the victim's employer?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence?
      `a competent authority has determined that I am a victim of trafficking or slavery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a competent authority determined that you are a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour?
      `my claim basis` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Are you claiming as a single claimant, as one of joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `I am responsible for any children or qualifying young persons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you responsible for any children or qualifying young persons?
      `any person is a non-dependant in relation to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is any person a non-dependant in relation to you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a specified renter` IF
    `Sch 4 para 28(1) — a specified renter` `me as a possible specified renter`
    WHERE
        `me as a possible specified renter` MEANS `Renter who may be a specified renter` WITH
            `claim basis` IS `my claim basis`
            `the renter as a possible excepted person` IS `my excepted person facts`
            `the renter is responsible for any children or qualifying young persons` IS `I am responsible for any children or qualifying young persons`
            `any person is a non-dependant in relation to the renter` IS `any person is a non-dependant in relation to me`
        `my excepted person facts` MEANS `Renter who may be an excepted person` WITH
            `age in complete years` IS `my age in complete years`
            `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related` IS `my home is in`
            `was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18` IS `I was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18`
            `stays in hostels` IS LIST `Stay in a hostel` WITH
                `the hostel` IS `Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` WITH
                    `the building as a possible hostel` IS `uc3 seat — a building that may be a hostel` `my home is in` `the building has accommodation that is not self-contained` `the building provides board` `the building provides facilities for preparing food` `the building is owned or managed by a local authority` `the building is owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the building is owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `the building is social housing` `the building is owned or managed by a registered social landlord` `the building is not run on a commercial basis` `the building is funded by government` `the building's manager is a public authority` `the building's manager is not run for profit` `the building's manager is a registered charity` `the building helps residents to be resettled` `the building is a care home` `the building is an independent hospital`
                    `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS `the main purpose of the hostel is accommodation with care, support or supervision for homeless people`
                `months the stay lasted` IS `the number of months I lived in that hostel`
                `whilst living in the hostel E was offered and has accepted services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to assist E to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS `while living in the hostel I was offered and accepted services to help me be resettled`
            payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for me`
                `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for me`
                `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for me`
                `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for me`
                `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for me`
                `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for me`
                `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for me`
            `active multi-agency management pursuant to arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS `I am subject to active multi-agency management under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`
            `active multi-agency risk management pursuant to arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act` IS `I am subject to active multi-agency risk management under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act`
            `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force` IS `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(b) or (d) is not fully in force`
            `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force` IS `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(e) is not fully in force`
            `considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS `the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large`
            `by reason of an offence of which they have been convicted, considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS `by reason of an offence I have been convicted of, the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large`
            `the renter as a possible holder of the foster parent condition` IS `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` WITH
                `the renter's placement of a child` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                    `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation in which the child is placed`
                    `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations`
                    `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
                `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them` IS `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now`
                `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent` IS YMD `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved`
                `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care`
                `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption` IS `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption`
            `after attaining the age of 16 had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them by their partner or former partner, or by a relative` IS `after attaining the age of 16 I had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me`
            `the person who provides evidence that the circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened` IS `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity` WITH
                `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person who gave evidence is a health care professional`
                `police officer` IS `the person who gave evidence is a police officer`
                `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person who gave evidence is a registered social worker`
                `the victim's employer` IS `the person who gave evidence is the victim's employer`
                `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence` IS `the person who gave evidence is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim`
            `the victim's circumstances are consistent with their having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them` IS `my circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me`
            `the person whom the victim has contacted in relation to such an incident` IS `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity` WITH
                `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a health care professional`
                `police officer` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a police officer`
                `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a registered social worker`
                `the victim's employer` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is the victim's employer`
                `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim`
            `a competent authority has determined that the renter is a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour` IS `a competent authority has determined that I am a victim of trafficking or slavery`

-- Sch 4 para 29. A renter (E) is "excepted" from the shared accommodation category if, for example, E is 18 to 24 and was a care leaver; is 16 to 34 and has lived at least 3 months in hostels for homeless
-- people and accepted services; is under 35 and receives one of the listed payments, is subject to active multi-agency management, satisfies the foster parent condition, has had domestic violence inflicted
-- (with evidence) or has been found a victim of trafficking. The seat takes the renter's stays in hostels as one stay (the months added together).
@export Am I an excepted person for the shared accommodation category (Sch 4 para 29)?
GIVEN `my age in complete years` IS A NUMBER @desc How old are you, in complete years?
      `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18?
      `the building has accommodation that is not self-contained` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building one where domestic accommodation is provided for people generally, or for a class of people, otherwise than in separate and self-contained premises?
      `the building provides board` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide board?
      `the building provides facilities for preparing food` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide facilities for preparing food adequate to the needs of those people?
      `the building is owned or managed by a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building owned or managed by a local authority?
      `the building is owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `the building is owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `the building is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building social housing?
      `the building is owned or managed by a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it owned or managed by a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `the building is not run on a commercial basis` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building operated other than on a commercial basis?
      `the building is funded by government` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are funds for the building provided wholly or in part by a government department or agency or a local authority?
      `the building's manager is a public authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manager of the building a public authority?
      `the building's manager is not run for profit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the manager of the building carry on its activities otherwise than for profit?
      `the building's manager is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the manager of the building a registered charity?
      `the building helps residents to be resettled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the building provide care, support or supervision with a view to helping the people there to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the building is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building a care home?
      `the building is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the building an independent hospital?
      `the main purpose of the hostel is accommodation with care, support or supervision for homeless people` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the main purpose of that building to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to helping them to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the number of months I lived in that hostel` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many months have you lived in hostels of that kind? (add together all your stays)
      `while living in the hostel I was offered and accepted services to help me be resettled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc While you lived there, were you offered and did you accept services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to help you to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community?
      `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `attendance allowance, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For attendance allowance: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `pension age disability payment, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For pension age disability payment: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of personal independence payment: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for me` IS A `Status of a disability payment` @desc For the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate: do you receive it, are you entitled to it but not receiving it, or neither? (received by the person; entitled to by the person but not received under the regulation listed for it; neither received nor so entitled)
      `I am subject to active multi-agency management under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to active multi-agency management under arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003?
      `I am subject to active multi-agency risk management under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you subject to active multi-agency risk management under arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the Management of Offenders etc. (Scotland) Act 2005?
      `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(b) or (d) is not fully in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 10(1) of the 2005 Act not apply to you only because section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force?
      `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(e) is not fully in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does section 10(1) of the 2005 Act not apply to you only because section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force?
      `the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Secretary of State consider you a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large?
      `by reason of an offence I have been convicted of, the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS A BOOLEAN @desc By reason of an offence of which you have been convicted, does the Secretary of State consider you a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large?
      `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a child placed with you under the placement regulations?
      `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you a foster carer or a kinship carer?
      `the nation in which the child is placed` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is the child placed? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Would you be a foster parent but for the fact that you do not currently have any child placed with you?
      `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you an adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption?
      `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month did your last placement end (or, if no child has yet been placed with you, were you approved to be a foster parent)? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year is the day you are asking about? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month is the day you are asking about? (1 to 31)
      `after attaining the age of 16 I had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc After attaining the age of 16, did your partner or former partner, or a relative, inflict domestic violence upon you or threaten you with it?
      `the person who gave evidence is a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person who gave evidence is a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a police officer?
      `the person who gave evidence is a registered social worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person who gave evidence is the victim's employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened the victim's employer?
      `the person who gave evidence is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person who provides evidence that your circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence?
      `my circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are your circumstances consistent with your having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against you?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a health care professional` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a police officer?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a registered social worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is the victim's employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident the victim's employer?
      `the person I contacted about the incident is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person whom you have contacted in relation to such an incident a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence?
      `a competent authority has determined that I am a victim of trafficking or slavery` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a competent authority determined that you are a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an excepted person for the shared accommodation category` IF
    `Sch 4 para 29(1) — an excepted person` `my excepted person facts`
    WHERE
        `my excepted person facts` MEANS `Renter who may be an excepted person` WITH
            `age in complete years` IS `my age in complete years`
            `nation of Great Britain to which the renter is related` IS `my home is in`
            `was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18` IS `I was a care leaver within the meaning of regulation 8 before reaching the age of 18`
            `stays in hostels` IS LIST `Stay in a hostel` WITH
                `the hostel` IS `Building that may be a hostel for homeless people` WITH
                    `the building as a possible hostel` IS `uc3 seat — a building that may be a hostel` `my home is in` `the building has accommodation that is not self-contained` `the building provides board` `the building provides facilities for preparing food` `the building is owned or managed by a local authority` `the building is owned or managed by a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `the building is owned or managed by a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `the building is social housing` `the building is owned or managed by a registered social landlord` `the building is not run on a commercial basis` `the building is funded by government` `the building's manager is a public authority` `the building's manager is not run for profit` `the building's manager is a registered charity` `the building helps residents to be resettled` `the building is a care home` `the building is an independent hospital`
                    `the main purpose of the building is to provide accommodation together with care, support or supervision for homeless people with a view to assisting such persons to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS `the main purpose of the hostel is accommodation with care, support or supervision for homeless people`
                `months the stay lasted` IS `the number of months I lived in that hostel`
                `whilst living in the hostel E was offered and has accepted services which the Secretary of State considers are intended to assist E to be rehabilitated or resettled within the community` IS `while living in the hostel I was offered and accepted services to help me be resettled`
            payments IS `Disability payments of a person` WITH
                `care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate` IS `the care component of disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate, for me`
                `care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11(5) of the DACYP Regulations` IS `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate, for me`
                `care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025` IS `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the highest or middle rate, for me`
                `attendance allowance` IS `attendance allowance, for me`
                `pension age disability payment` IS `pension age disability payment, for me`
                `daily living component of personal independence payment` IS `the daily living component of personal independence payment, for me`
                `daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate` IS `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate, for me`
            `active multi-agency management pursuant to arrangements established by a responsible authority under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS `I am subject to active multi-agency management under section 325(2) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`
            `active multi-agency risk management pursuant to arrangements established by the responsible authorities under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act` IS `I am subject to active multi-agency risk management under section 10(1) of the 2005 Act`
            `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(b) or (d) has not been brought fully into force` IS `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(b) or (d) is not fully in force`
            `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply by reason only of the fact that section 10(1)(e) has not been brought fully into force` IS `section 10(1) of the 2005 Act does not apply only because section 10(1)(e) is not fully in force`
            `considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS `the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large`
            `by reason of an offence of which they have been convicted, considered by the Secretary of State to be a person who may cause serious harm to the public at large` IS `by reason of an offence I have been convicted of, the Secretary of State considers I may cause serious harm to the public at large`
            `the renter as a possible holder of the foster parent condition` IS `Renter who may satisfy the foster parent condition` WITH
                `the renter's placement of a child` IS `Placement of a child with a person` WITH
                    `nation in which the child is placed` IS `the nation in which the child is placed`
                    `child is placed with the person under the placement regulations` IS `I have a child placed with me under the placement regulations`
                    `person is a foster carer or a kinship carer` IS `I am a foster carer or a kinship carer`
                `the renter would be a foster parent but for the fact that they do not currently have any child placed with them` IS `I would be a foster parent but for having no child placed with me now`
                `the day the renter's last placement ended or, if no child has yet been placed with them, the day on which they were approved to be a foster parent` IS YMD `the year of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved` `the day of the month of the day my last placement ended or I was approved`
                `day to which the determination relates` IS YMD `the year of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the month of the day I am asking about for foster care` `the day of the month of the day I am asking about for foster care`
                `adopter with whom a child has been placed for adoption` IS `I am an adopter with a child placed with me for adoption`
            `after attaining the age of 16 had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them by their partner or former partner, or by a relative` IS `after attaining the age of 16 I had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me`
            `the person who provides evidence that the circumstances are consistent with domestic violence having been inflicted or threatened` IS `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity` WITH
                `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person who gave evidence is a health care professional`
                `police officer` IS `the person who gave evidence is a police officer`
                `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person who gave evidence is a registered social worker`
                `the victim's employer` IS `the person who gave evidence is the victim's employer`
                `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence` IS `the person who gave evidence is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim`
            `the victim's circumstances are consistent with their having had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them` IS `my circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened against me`
            `the person whom the victim has contacted in relation to such an incident` IS `Person who may be a person acting in an official capacity` WITH
                `health care professional within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a health care professional`
                `police officer` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a police officer`
                `registered social worker within the meaning given by regulation 98(4)` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a registered social worker`
                `the victim's employer` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is the victim's employer`
                `a public, voluntary, or charitable body which has had direct contact with the victim in connection with domestic violence` IS `the person I contacted about the incident is a public, voluntary or charitable body that has had direct contact with the victim`
            `a competent authority has determined that the renter is a victim of trafficking in human beings, slavery, servitude or forced or compulsory labour` IS `a competent authority has determined that I am a victim of trafficking or slavery`

-- Sch 4 paras 20 and 30. Part 4 (the private rented sector) applies to a renter who is liable to make rent payments to a person other than a provider of social housing; Part 5 (the social rented
-- sector) to a renter who is liable to make rent payments to a provider of social housing. Either way it is irrelevant whether the renter is also liable for service charge payments.
@export Is my landlord a provider of social housing, so that Part 5 of Schedule 4 applies to me (Sch 4 para 30)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `my landlord is a local authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a local authority?
      `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a non-profit registered provider of social housing?
      `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a profit-making registered provider of social housing?
      `my home is social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home social housing?
      `my landlord is a registered social landlord` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your landlord a registered social landlord (on the Welsh Ministers' or the Scottish Housing Regulator's register)?
      `I am also liable to make service charge payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you also liable to make service charge payments?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my landlord a provider of social housing so that Part 5 of Schedule 4 applies to me` IF
    `Sch 4 para 30 — Part 5 applies to the renter` `my renting`
    WHERE
        `my renting` MEANS `Renter whose landlord decides the Part` WITH
            `the landlord that rent payments are payable to` IS `uc3 seat — a landlord that may be a provider of social housing` `my home is in` `my landlord is a local authority` `my landlord is a non-profit registered provider of social housing` `my landlord is a profit-making registered provider of social housing` `my home is social housing` `my landlord is a registered social landlord`
            `the renter is also liable to make service charge payments` IS `I am also liable to make service charge payments`

-- Sch 4 paras 31 to 36, 33 to 35. Under Part 5 (the social rented sector) the housing costs element is amount S less the housing cost contributions. S is the monthly total of the relevant payments (after
-- adding back a tenant incentive scheme reduction, deducting an amount that relates to a commodity, and using a rent officer's lower amount unless it is not appropriate) less any under-occupation deduction;
-- for joint tenants it is a share of that total. The service charge, if any, is taken with no tenant incentive scheme reduction and no rent officer determination (a limit of this question, not of the Schedule), and as a payment that meets every paragraph 8 condition.
@export What is my housing costs element if I rent from a social landlord (Sch 4 paras 31 to 36)?
GIVEN `the amount of each rent payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each rent payment, in pounds? (0 if there is none)
      `how often the rent falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the rent fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my rent arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for the rent provide for one or more periods in which it is not payable?
      `the total number of rent payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many rent payments are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `the reduction applied to my rent under a tenant incentive scheme` IS A NUMBER @desc What reduction in your rent has been applied by a provider of social housing under a tenant incentive scheme, in pounds? (0 if none)
      `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing to avoid rent arrears` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme operated by a provider of social housing and designed to avoid rent arrears by allowing reductions in rent or service charges or other advantages in return for meeting specified conditions?
      `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme approved by the Secretary of State?
      `the amount of my rent that relates to a commodity` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your rent, in pounds, relates to the supply of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by a member of your extended benefit unit? (0 if none)
      `a rent officer has determined a lower amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a rent officer determined that a landlord might reasonably have expected to obtain a lower amount of rent?
      `the lower amount the rent officer determined` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what lower amount did the rent officer determine, in pounds?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it is not appropriate to use that lower amount?
      `the amount of each service charge payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each service charge payment, in pounds? (0 if there is none)
      `how often the service charge falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does the service charge fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my service charge arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for the service charge provide for one or more periods in which it is not payable?
      `the total number of service charge payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many service charge payments are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `the amount of my service charge that relates to a commodity` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of your service charge, in pounds, relates to the supply of a commodity (such as water or fuel) for use by a member of your extended benefit unit? (0 if none)
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for these payments?
      `these payments have already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have these payments already been brought into account, for you or another renter?
      `the number of bedrooms in my home` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are there in your home?
      `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) apply to you?
      `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has domestic violence been inflicted upon or threatened against you or a member of your extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative?
      `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the victim not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence?
      `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of your extended benefit unit?
      `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity (regulation 98(4)) that you are living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme?
      `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme one operated by a provider of social housing to enable victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security?
      `the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the victim's circumstances consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them?
      `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the victim made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident?
      `the number of bedrooms I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are you entitled to under paragraphs 8 to 12? (see the bedrooms question above)
      `the number of listed persons liable for the payments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the people liable to make the payments are you, your partner, or a child or qualifying young person you are responsible for? (the listed persons)
      `the number of other persons liable for the payments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many other people are liable to make the payments with you?
      `the Secretary of State is satisfied that sharing the payments by number of people would be unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Secretary of State satisfied that it would be unreasonable to share the payments according to the number of people liable?
      `the amount the Secretary of State considers appropriate` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, what amount does the Secretary of State consider appropriate in all the circumstances, in pounds? (0 if not applicable)
      `the housing cost contributions to be deducted` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the sum of the housing cost contributions to be deducted, in pounds? (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my housing costs element if I rent from a social landlord` IS
    `Sch 4 para 33 — the amount of the renter's housing costs element under Part 5` `amount S` `the housing cost contributions to be deducted`
    WHERE
        `amount S` MEANS `Sch 4 para 35 — amount S for joint tenants` `our joint liability` `my under-occupation facts` `the number of bedrooms I am entitled to`
        `our joint liability` MEANS `Joint liability in the social rented sector` WITH
            `relevant payments of the renter and of the others in respect of the accommodation taken as a whole` IS LIST `uc3 seat — a relevant payment in the social rented sector` (`uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` FALSE FALSE `the amount of each rent payment` `how often the rent falls due` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` `my rent arrangements provide for free periods` `the total number of rent payments in the 12 month period`) `the reduction applied to my rent under a tenant incentive scheme` `the scheme is operated by a provider of social housing to avoid rent arrears` `the scheme is approved by the Secretary of State` `the amount of my rent that relates to a commodity` `a rent officer has determined a lower amount` `the lower amount the rent officer determined` `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it is not appropriate to use the lower amount`, `uc3 seat — a relevant payment in the social rented sector` (`uc3 seat — a liability for a payment` TRUE TRUE `the amount of each service charge payment` `how often the service charge falls due` `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for these payments` `these payments have already been brought into account` `my service charge arrangements provide for free periods` `the total number of service charge payments in the 12 month period`) 0 FALSE FALSE `the amount of my service charge that relates to a commodity` FALSE 0 FALSE
            `number of listed persons liable to make relevant payments` IS `the number of listed persons liable for the payments`
            `number of other persons liable to make relevant payments` IS `the number of other persons liable for the payments`
            `the Secretary of State is satisfied that it would be unreasonable to determine amount S in accordance with sub-paragraph (4)` IS `the Secretary of State is satisfied that sharing the payments by number of people would be unreasonable`
            `amount S determined in such manner as the Secretary of State considers appropriate in all the circumstances` IS `the amount the Secretary of State considers appropriate`
        `my under-occupation facts` MEANS `uc3 seat — the facts for an under-occupation deduction` `the number of bedrooms in my home` `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit` `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it` `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit` `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` `the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened` `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident`

-- Sch 4 para 36(1), (5), (6). A deduction for under-occupation is made where the bedrooms in the accommodation exceed the bedrooms the renter is entitled to, unless regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership)
-- applies or the renter has had domestic violence inflicted or threatened and lives in a sanctuary scheme property (the facts of paragraph 36(6)).
@export Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to (Sch 4 para 36)?
GIVEN `the number of bedrooms in my home` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are there in your home?
      `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) apply to you?
      `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has domestic violence been inflicted upon or threatened against you or a member of your extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative?
      `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the victim not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence?
      `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of your extended benefit unit?
      `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity (regulation 98(4)) that you are living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme?
      `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme one operated by a provider of social housing to enable victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security?
      `the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the victim's circumstances consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them?
      `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the victim made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident?
      `the number of bedrooms I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are you entitled to under paragraphs 8 to 12? (see the bedrooms question above)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will a deduction be made because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` IF
    `Sch 4 para 36(1) — a deduction for under-occupation is to be made` `my under-occupation facts` `the number of bedrooms I am entitled to`
    WHERE
        `my under-occupation facts` MEANS `uc3 seat — the facts for an under-occupation deduction` `the number of bedrooms in my home` `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit` `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it` `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit` `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` `the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened` `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident`

-- Sch 4 para 36(2) to (4). Where a deduction is made it is a percentage of the monthly total of the relevant payments: 14% for one excess bedroom and 25% for two or more.
@export How much will be deducted because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to (Sch 4 para 36)?
GIVEN `the number of bedrooms in my home` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are there in your home?
      `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership) apply to you?
      `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has domestic violence been inflicted upon or threatened against you or a member of your extended benefit unit by that person's partner or former partner, or by a relative?
      `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the victim not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened the domestic violence?
      `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is that person a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of your extended benefit unit?
      `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity (regulation 98(4)) that you are living in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme?
      `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the scheme one operated by a provider of social housing to enable victims of domestic violence to remain in their homes through the installation of additional security?
      `the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the victim's circumstances consistent with those of a person who has had domestic violence inflicted upon or threatened against them?
      `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the victim made contact with the person acting in an official capacity in relation to such an incident?
      `the number of bedrooms I am entitled to` IS A NUMBER @desc How many bedrooms are you entitled to under paragraphs 8 to 12? (see the bedrooms question above)
      `the monthly total of my relevant payments` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the monthly total of your relevant payments, in pounds?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much will be deducted because I have more bedrooms than I am entitled to` IS
    `Sch 4 para 36(2) — the amount of the under-occupation deduction` `my under-occupation facts` `the number of bedrooms I am entitled to` `the monthly total of my relevant payments`
    WHERE
        `my under-occupation facts` MEANS `uc3 seat — the facts for an under-occupation deduction` `the number of bedrooms in my home` `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` `domestic violence has been inflicted or threatened against me or a member of my extended benefit unit` `the victim is not living at the same address as the person who inflicted or threatened it` `that person is a qualifying young person who is a dependant of a member of my extended benefit unit` `I provide evidence from a person acting in an official capacity that I live in a property adapted under a sanctuary scheme` `the sanctuary scheme is operated by a provider of social housing` `the victim's circumstances are consistent with having had domestic violence inflicted or threatened` `the victim has made contact with the person acting in an official capacity about such an incident`

§§ `Schedule 5 -- housing costs element for owner-occupiers`


-- Sch 5 para 1. Schedule 5 is about claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies, who are called "owner-occupiers"; "joint owner-occupiers" are joint claimants to whom regulation 26(3) applies.
-- Whether regulation 26(3) applies is outside this range and is taken as a fact the person states.
@export Am I an owner-occupier for the housing costs element (Sch 5 para 1)?
GIVEN `regulation 26(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 26(3) apply to you (the regulation that says who is treated as an owner-occupier)?
      `my claim basis` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Are you claiming as a single claimant, as one of joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I an owner-occupier for the housing costs element` IF
    `Sch 5 para 1(2) — a claimant is an owner-occupier` `me as a possible owner-occupier`
    WHERE
        `me as a possible owner-occupier` MEANS `Claimant who may be an owner-occupier` WITH
            `regulation 26(3) applies to the claimant` IS `regulation 26(3) applies to me`
            `claim basis` IS `my claim basis`

@export Am I a joint owner-occupier for the housing costs element (Sch 5 para 1)?
GIVEN `regulation 26(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does regulation 26(3) apply to you (the regulation that says who is treated as an owner-occupier)?
      `my claim basis` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Are you claiming as a single claimant, as one of joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a joint owner-occupier for the housing costs element` IF
    `Sch 5 para 1(2) — a joint owner-occupier` `me as a possible owner-occupier`
    WHERE
        `me as a possible owner-occupier` MEANS `Claimant who may be an owner-occupier` WITH
            `regulation 26(3) applies to the claimant` IS `regulation 26(3) applies to me`
            `claim basis` IS `my claim basis`


-- Sch 5 para 3. The relevant payments of an owner-occupier are the service charge payments, as paragraphs 7 and 8 of Schedule 1 understand them. The housing costs element of an owner-occupier is calculated
-- under Schedule 5, so the paragraph 8 conditions that apply where it is calculated under Schedule 5 apply, and so does the limb of category A of paragraph 8(4) for a claimant whose housing costs element
-- falls to be calculated under Schedule 5; this question does not ask about either.
@export Is what I pay a relevant payment for the housing costs element of an owner-occupier (Sch 5 para 3)?
GIVEN `my home is in` IS A `Nation of Great Britain` @desc In which nation of Great Britain is your home? (England, Wales or Scotland)
      `what I pay is partly for services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay, in whole or in part, a payment towards the costs of services or facilities for the use or benefit of the people living in your home?
      `what I pay is fairly attributable to services or facilities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay, in whole or in part, fairly attributable to the cost of such services or facilities?
      `a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a qualifying loan under the Loans for Mortgage Interest Regulations 2017 taken out to make these payments?
      `my home is a tent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home a tent?
      `my home is approved premises` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home approved premises?
      `my home is a care home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home a care home?
      `my home is an independent hospital` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home an independent hospital?
      `my home is exempt accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your home exempt accommodation?
      `the right to occupy depends on making the payments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is making these payments a condition on which your right to occupy your home depends?
      `the payments are for external window cleaning` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for the external cleaning of windows?
      `the windows are in upper floors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so, are the windows in the upper floors of a multi-storey building?
      `the payments are for other maintenance or repair` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for other internal or external maintenance or repair of your home?
      `the payments for repair are separately identifiable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments separately identifiable as relating to that maintenance or repair?
      `I occupy under a shared ownership tenancy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you occupy your home under a shared ownership tenancy?
      `the payments are for communal areas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for ongoing maintenance or cleaning of, or the supply of water, fuel or any other commodity to, internal or external areas of communal use (including reasonable facilities such as laundry rooms or children's play areas)?
      `the payments are for basic communal services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments for the provision, ongoing maintenance, cleaning or repair of basic services available to everyone living in the accommodation (such as refuse collection, communal lifts, secure building access or aerials)?
      `the payments are for essential items in my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments specific to your home and limited to the use of essential items in it (such as furniture or domestic appliances)?
      `the costs are of a reasonable amount` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the costs and charges the payments relate to of a reasonable amount?
      `the services are of a reasonable description` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the costs and charges relate to services or facilities of a description that it is reasonable to provide?
      `public funds might otherwise pay for the services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the payments relate to services or facilities for which payments out of public funds might otherwise be made?
      `the payments transfer an asset` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are the payments in connection with the use of an asset and do they result in the transfer of the asset or any interest in it?
      `the payments are for food or medical or personal services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the payments relate to the cost of providing food, medical services or personal services (including personal care)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I pay a relevant payment for the housing costs element of an owner-occupier` IF
    `Sch 5 para 3 — the payment is a relevant payment` `my payment`
    WHERE
        `my payment` MEANS `uc3 seat — a payment that may be a service charge payment` `what I pay is partly for services or facilities` `what I pay is fairly attributable to services or facilities` `a mortgage interest loan was taken out for what I pay` `my home` `the paragraph 8 facts`
        `my home` MEANS `uc3 seat — a home as the Schedule 1 tests look at it` `my home is in` `my home is a tent` `my home is approved premises` `my home is a care home` `my home is an independent hospital` `my home is exempt accommodation`
        `the paragraph 8 facts` MEANS `uc3 seat — the paragraph 8 facts about a payment` TRUE `the right to occupy depends on making the payments` `the payments are for external window cleaning` `the windows are in upper floors` `the payments are for other maintenance or repair` `the payments for repair are separately identifiable` `I occupy under a shared ownership tenancy` TRUE `the payments are for communal areas` `the payments are for basic communal services` `the payments are for essential items in my home` `the costs are of a reasonable amount` `the services are of a reasonable description` `public funds might otherwise pay for the services` `the payments transfer an asset` `the payments are for food or medical or personal services`


-- Sch 5 para 4. Section 11(1) of the Act (housing costs) does not apply to an owner-occupier for an assessment period in which they, or either member of a couple, have any earned income, however small and whatever
-- the work (sub-paragraph (2) makes the nature of the work, its duration and the amount irrelevant: they are placeholders below). Whether income is earned income is outside this range and is the person's answer.
@export Do I get no housing costs element as an owner-occupier for an assessment period because someone has earned income (Sch 5 para 4)?
GIVEN `my claim basis` IS A `Claim basis` @desc Are you claiming as a single claimant, as one of joint claimants, or as a single claimant who is a member of a couple?
      `I have any earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have any earned income in the assessment period?
      `the other member of my couple has any earned income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you are a member of a couple, does the other member have any earned income in the assessment period?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I get no housing costs element as an owner-occupier for an assessment period because someone has earned income` IF
    `Sch 5 para 4 — section 11(1) of the Act does not apply to the owner-occupier for the assessment period` `my earnings`
    WHERE
        `my earnings` MEANS `Owner-occupier's earned income in an assessment period` WITH
            `claim basis` IS `my claim basis`
            `the owner-occupier has any earned income` IS `I have any earned income`
            `the other member of the couple has any earned income` IS `the other member of my couple has any earned income`
            -- Placeholders: sub-paragraph (2) makes these irrelevant, and no rule reads them.
            `the nature of the work engaged in` IS ""
            `the duration of the work` IS 0
            `the amount of the earned income` IS 0

-- Sch 5 para 4(3). Paragraph 4 does not stop an amount calculated under Schedule 4 from being included in the award of a claimant who falls within regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership).
@export Can an amount under Schedule 4 still be included for me despite earned income because of shared ownership (Sch 5 para 4)?
GIVEN `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you fall within regulation 26(4) to (6) (shared ownership)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can an amount under Schedule 4 still be included for me despite earned income because of shared ownership` IF
    `Sch 5 para 4(3) — paragraph 4 does not prevent an amount calculated under Schedule 4 from being included` `regulation 26(4) to (6) applies to me`


-- Sch 5 para 5. An owner-occupier's award does not include an amount calculated under Schedule 5 until the assessment period after the one in which the qualifying period ends. The qualifying period is 9
-- consecutive assessment periods in which the person has been receiving universal credit and would otherwise qualify (a new award), or in which they would otherwise qualify (an award from which an amount has
-- ceased to be included). A period that does not count stops the qualifying period running, and a new one starts when the requirements are met again. Paragraph 6(2) and paragraph 7(2) add periods to the count.
@export Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier (Sch 5 para 5)?
GIVEN `my qualifying period is for` IS A `Kind of qualifying period` @desc Is your qualifying period for a new award, or for an award from which an amount calculated under Schedule 5 has ceased to be included?
      `the number of assessment periods in a row, not counting this one, that count towards my qualifying period` IS A NUMBER @desc Not counting this assessment period, how many assessment periods in a row count towards your qualifying period (you have been receiving universal credit and would otherwise qualify for an amount under Schedule 5; for an award from which an amount has ceased to be included, the second condition alone)? (only the run since the last period that did not count; 9 is the most that matters)
      `the assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many assessment periods are credited to you under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward to you under paragraph 7(2)? (see the questions below; 0 if none)
      `paragraph 7(3) applies to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an amount calculated under Schedule 5 already included in the award that ended, so that paragraph 7(3) applies to your further award?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I got past the qualifying period for the housing costs element as an owner-occupier` IF
    `Sch 5 para 5 — the owner-occupier is past the qualifying period` `my qualifying period facts`
    WHERE
        `my qualifying period facts` MEANS `Facts about the qualifying period` WITH
            `kind of qualifying period` IS `my qualifying period is for`
            `assessment periods, oldest first, ending with the one in question` IS append (`uc3 seat — a run of counting assessment periods` `the number of assessment periods in a row, not counting this one, that count towards my qualifying period`) (LIST `uc3 seat — the assessment period in question`)
            `assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2)` IS `the assessment periods credited under paragraph 6(2) or carried forward under paragraph 7(2)`
            `paragraph 7(3) applies: an amount calculated under this Schedule was already included in the award that ended` IS `paragraph 7(3) applies to me`


-- Sch 5 para 6(2). An owner-occupier who was entitled to a jobseeker's allowance or an employment and support allowance immediately before the award began has the days on which they received it, in a period made
-- up only of such days, treated as if they were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods: the number of days divided by the days in an assessment period (a part of a period is a fraction: fork U3-F25).
@export How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as (Sch 5 para 6)?
GIVEN `I was entitled to a jobseeker's allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to a jobseeker's allowance immediately before your award of universal credit began?
      `I was entitled to an employment and support allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you entitled to an employment and support allowance immediately before your award of universal credit began?
      `the number of days on which I received that benefit in the period` IS A NUMBER @desc On how many days in the period did you receive that benefit?
      `the period comprises only days on which I was receiving that benefit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the period comprise only days on which you were receiving that benefit?
      `the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the period treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods?
      `the year of the first day of my assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was the first day of your assessment period? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the first day of my assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month was the first day of your assessment period? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the first day of my assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the first day of your assessment period? (1 to 31)
      `the year of the last day of my assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year was the last day of your assessment period? (for example 2025)
      `the month of the last day of my assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month was the last day of your assessment period? (1 to 12)
      `the day of the month of the last day of my assessment period` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the last day of your assessment period? (1 to 31)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many assessment periods do my days of jobseeker's allowance or employment and support allowance count as` IS
    `Sch 5 para 6(2) — the assessment periods that the days of benefit are treated as` `my benefit days`
    WHERE
        `my benefit days` MEANS `Owner-occupier entitled to a jobseeker's allowance or an employment and support allowance` WITH
            `immediately before the commencement of the award of universal credit the owner-occupier is entitled to a jobseeker's allowance` IS `I was entitled to a jobseeker's allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began`
            `immediately before the commencement of the award of universal credit the owner-occupier is entitled to an employment and support allowance` IS `I was entitled to an employment and support allowance immediately before my award of universal credit began`
            `number of days on which the owner-occupier was receiving that benefit in the period` IS `the number of days on which I received that benefit in the period`
            `the period comprises only days on which the owner-occupier was receiving that benefit` IS `the period comprises only days on which I was receiving that benefit`
            `the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods` IS `the period is treated as if it were the whole or part of one or more assessment periods`
            `the assessment period used for the count` IS `Assessment period` WITH
                `first day` IS YMD `the year of the first day of my assessment period` `the month of the first day of my assessment period` `the day of the month of the first day of my assessment period`
                `last day` IS YMD `the year of the last day of my assessment period` `the month of the last day of my assessment period` `the day of the month of the last day of my assessment period`


-- Sch 5 para 7. Where an award to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple and a further award is made to one or each of them for the same home, the whole or part of any assessment
-- period that would have counted under the terminated award is carried forward to the further award.
@export Does paragraph 7 carry my assessment periods forward after my partner and I stop being a couple (Sch 5 para 7)?
GIVEN `our award of universal credit as joint owner-occupiers was terminated because we ceased to be a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an award of universal credit to you and your partner as joint owner-occupiers terminated because you ceased to be a couple?
      `a further award was made to one of us or to each of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a further award made to one of you (or to each of you)?
      `for the further award the occupation condition is met for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In relation to the further award, is the occupation condition met in respect of the same accommodation as the one you occupied together as your home?
      `the number of assessment periods that would have counted under the terminated award` IS A NUMBER @desc How many assessment periods (or parts of them, as a fraction) would have counted in relation to the award that was terminated?
      `the further award was made on a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the further award made on a claim?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does paragraph 7 carry my assessment periods forward after my partner and I stop being a couple` IF
    `Sch 5 para 7(1) — this paragraph applies` `our further award`
    WHERE
        `our further award` MEANS `Further award after joint owner-occupiers cease to be a couple` WITH
            `an award of universal credit to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple` IS `our award of universal credit as joint owner-occupiers was terminated because we ceased to be a couple`
            `a further award is made to one of them (or to each of them)` IS `a further award was made to one of us or to each of us`
            `in relation to the further award the occupation condition is met in respect of the same accommodation as that occupied by the joint owner-occupiers as their home` IS `for the further award the occupation condition is met for the same home`
            `assessment periods which would have counted in relation to the award that is terminated` IS `the number of assessment periods that would have counted under the terminated award`
            `the further award is made on a claim` IS `the further award was made on a claim`

@export How many assessment periods are carried forward to my further award after my partner and I stop being a couple (Sch 5 para 7)?
GIVEN `our award of universal credit as joint owner-occupiers was terminated because we ceased to be a couple` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was an award of universal credit to you and your partner as joint owner-occupiers terminated because you ceased to be a couple?
      `a further award was made to one of us or to each of us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was a further award made to one of you (or to each of you)?
      `for the further award the occupation condition is met for the same home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In relation to the further award, is the occupation condition met in respect of the same accommodation as the one you occupied together as your home?
      `the number of assessment periods that would have counted under the terminated award` IS A NUMBER @desc How many assessment periods (or parts of them, as a fraction) would have counted in relation to the award that was terminated?
      `the further award was made on a claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the further award made on a claim?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many assessment periods are carried forward to my further award after my partner and I stop being a couple` IS
    `Sch 5 para 7(2) — the assessment periods carried forward to the further award` `our further award`
    WHERE
        `our further award` MEANS `Further award after joint owner-occupiers cease to be a couple` WITH
            `an award of universal credit to joint owner-occupiers is terminated because they cease to be a couple` IS `our award of universal credit as joint owner-occupiers was terminated because we ceased to be a couple`
            `a further award is made to one of them (or to each of them)` IS `a further award was made to one of us or to each of us`
            `in relation to the further award the occupation condition is met in respect of the same accommodation as that occupied by the joint owner-occupiers as their home` IS `for the further award the occupation condition is met for the same home`
            `assessment periods which would have counted in relation to the award that is terminated` IS `the number of assessment periods that would have counted under the terminated award`
            `the further award is made on a claim` IS `the further award was made on a claim`


-- Sch 5 paras 9 and 13. The housing costs element of an owner-occupier is the monthly amount of the service charge payments taken into account under paragraph 8: ones that are relevant payments (Sch 5 para 3), for which
-- the person meets the payment, liability and occupation conditions, once the qualifying period has ended, and not already brought into account. A payment is brought to a monthly amount as for Schedule 4 paragraph 7
-- (the text's formulas for the number of payments where there are service charge free periods, in paragraph 13(4A), are missing from this rendering: the number is an input).
-- These questions take it that what you pay is a service charge payment that meets Schedule 1 paragraph 8 (ask the question above), and take at most two such service charges.
@export What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier (Sch 5 paras 9 and 13)?
GIVEN `the amount of each first service charge payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each payment of your first service charge, in pounds? (0 if you have none)
      `how often the first service charge falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does your first service charge fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for your first service charge provide for one or more service charge free periods?
      `the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many payments of it are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for your first service charge?
      `the first service charge has already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your first service charge already been brought into account, for you or another owner-occupier?
      `the amount of each second service charge payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each payment of your second service charge, in pounds? (0 if you have none)
      `how often the second service charge falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does your second service charge fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my second service charge arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for your second service charge provide for one or more service charge free periods?
      `the total number of second service charge payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many payments of it are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for your second service charge?
      `the second service charge has already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your second service charge already been brought into account, for you or another owner-occupier?
      `the qualifying period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your qualifying period ended, so that Schedule 5 can include an amount (see the question above)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is my housing costs element as an owner-occupier` IS
    `Sch 5 para 9 — the amount of the owner-occupier's housing costs element` (LIST `my first service charge`, `my second service charge`)
    WHERE
        `my first service charge` MEANS `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment` WITH
                payment IS `uc3 seat — a service charge payment that meets paragraph 8`
                `amount of each payment in pounds` IS `the amount of each first service charge payment`
                `how often the payment falls due` IS `how often the first service charge falls due`
                `the owner-occupier meets the payment condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge`
                `the owner-occupier meets the liability condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge`
                `the owner-occupier meets the occupation condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge`
                `the qualifying period has ended` IS `the qualifying period has ended`
                `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier` IS `the first service charge has already been brought into account`
                `the arrangements provide for one or more service charge free periods` IS `my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods`
                `total number of the service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS `the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period`
        `my second service charge` MEANS `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment` WITH
                payment IS `uc3 seat — a service charge payment that meets paragraph 8`
                `amount of each payment in pounds` IS `the amount of each second service charge payment`
                `how often the payment falls due` IS `how often the second service charge falls due`
                `the owner-occupier meets the payment condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge`
                `the owner-occupier meets the liability condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge`
                `the owner-occupier meets the occupation condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the second service charge`
                `the qualifying period has ended` IS `the qualifying period has ended`
                `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier` IS `the second service charge has already been brought into account`
                `the arrangements provide for one or more service charge free periods` IS `my second service charge arrangements provide for free periods`
                `total number of the service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS `the total number of second service charge payments in the 12 month period`

@export Is what I pay as an owner-occupier taken into account for my housing costs element (Sch 5 para 8)?
GIVEN `what I pay is a service charge payment that meets Schedule 1 paragraph 8` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is what you pay a service charge payment that meets Schedule 1 paragraph 8 (see the Schedule 1 question above)?
      `the amount of each first service charge payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each payment of your first service charge, in pounds? (0 if you have none)
      `how often the first service charge falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does your first service charge fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for your first service charge provide for one or more service charge free periods?
      `the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many payments of it are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
      `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you meet the payment condition, the liability condition and the occupation condition (regulation 25(5)) for your first service charge?
      `the first service charge has already been brought into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your first service charge already been brought into account, for you or another owner-occupier?
      `the qualifying period has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has your qualifying period ended, so that Schedule 5 can include an amount (see the question above)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is what I pay as an owner-occupier taken into account for my housing costs element` IF
    `Sch 5 para 8 — the payment is taken into account` `my first service charge`
    WHERE
        `my first service charge` MEANS `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment` WITH
                payment IS (IF `what I pay is a service charge payment that meets Schedule 1 paragraph 8` THEN `uc3 seat — a service charge payment that meets paragraph 8` ELSE `uc3 seat — a payment that is not a service charge payment`)
                `amount of each payment in pounds` IS `the amount of each first service charge payment`
                `how often the payment falls due` IS `how often the first service charge falls due`
                `the owner-occupier meets the payment condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge`
                `the owner-occupier meets the liability condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge`
                `the owner-occupier meets the occupation condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS `I meet the payment, liability and occupation conditions for the first service charge`
                `the qualifying period has ended` IS `the qualifying period has ended`
                `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier` IS `the first service charge has already been brought into account`
                `the arrangements provide for one or more service charge free periods` IS `my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods`
                `total number of the service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS `the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period`

@export What is the monthly amount of my service charge as an owner-occupier (Sch 5 para 13)?
GIVEN `the amount of each first service charge payment` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the amount of each payment of your first service charge, in pounds? (0 if you have none)
      `how often the first service charge falls due` IS A `Payment interval` @desc How often does your first service charge fall due? (weekly payments, two-weekly payments, four-weekly payments, monthly payments, three-monthly payments or annual payments)
      `my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do your arrangements for your first service charge provide for one or more service charge free periods?
      `the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period` IS A NUMBER @desc If so, how many payments of it are you liable to make in the 12 month period?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the monthly amount of my service charge as an owner-occupier` IS
    `Sch 5 para 13 — the monthly amount of a service charge payment` `my first service charge`
    WHERE
        `my first service charge` MEANS `Liability of an owner-occupier for a service charge payment` WITH
            payment IS `uc3 seat — a service charge payment that meets paragraph 8`
            `amount of each payment in pounds` IS `the amount of each first service charge payment`
            `how often the payment falls due` IS `how often the first service charge falls due`
            -- Placeholders: the monthly amount reads only the amount, the interval, the free periods flag and the number of payments.
            `the owner-occupier meets the payment condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS TRUE
            `the owner-occupier meets the liability condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS TRUE
            `the owner-occupier meets the occupation condition in respect of the relevant payment` IS TRUE
            `the qualifying period has ended` IS TRUE
            `the payment has already been brought into account in relation to the same or a different owner-occupier` IS FALSE
            `the arrangements provide for one or more service charge free periods` IS `my first service charge arrangements provide for free periods`
            `total number of the service charge payments which the owner-occupier is liable to make in that 12 month period` IS `the total number of first service charge payments in the 12 month period`

-- Sch 5 para 13(5). A service charge free period is a period in which the owner-occupier has no liability to make one or more of the service charge payments taken into account under paragraph 8.
@export Is this period a service charge free period for me (Sch 5 para 13)?
GIVEN `I have no liability in this period to make one or more of my service charge payments that are taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In this period, do you have no liability to make one or more of the service charge payments that are taken into account under paragraph 8?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this period a service charge free period for me` IF
    `Sch 5 para 13(5) — a service charge free period` `this period`
    WHERE
        `this period` MEANS `Period of the arrangements for service charge payments` WITH
            `the owner-occupier has no liability in respect of the period to make one or more of the service charge payments which are to be taken into account under paragraph 8` IS `I have no liability in this period to make one or more of my service charge payments that are taken into account`


§§ `Schedule 5A -- claimants who had limited capability for work and work-related activity before 6 April 2026`


-- Sch 5A para 1. A claimant is a pre-2026 claimant if they have limited capability for work and work-related activity, are entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element by virtue of one of paragraphs 2 to 5, and have been
-- so entitled continuously since the element was included. Paragraphs 2 to 5 compare each day with 6 April 2026 and nothing else, so each "on a day before (or on or after) 6 April 2026" is a yes or no here; the layer-1 rules
-- are given the stand-in day 5 April 2026 (before) or 6 April 2026 (on or after) and the real day is never needed. Nothing reads the route by which the decision was made, or the claimant's severe conditions criteria and limited capability for work.
@export Am I a pre-2026 claimant for the LCWRA element (Sch 5A)?
GIVEN `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `my award of universal credit includes the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element?
      `I have been so entitled continuously since the LCWRA element was included` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been so entitled continuously from the time the LCWRA element was included in your award?
      `before 6 April 2026 I was awaiting an assessment under Part 5 (regulation 41(1)(a))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day before 6 April 2026 were you, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), awaiting an assessment under Part 5?
      `on or after 6 April 2026 I was found to have LCWRA and entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element (case 2)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day on or after 6 April 2026, were you determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and was a decision made that you are entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element?
      `before 6 April 2026 I had limited capability for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day before 6 April 2026 did you have limited capability for work?
      `before 6 April 2026 I was awaiting a further assessment under Part 5 (regulation 41(1)(b))` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day before 6 April 2026 were you, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(b), awaiting a further assessment under Part 5?
      `on or after 6 April 2026 I was found to have LCWRA and entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element (case 3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day on or after 6 April 2026, were you determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and was a decision made that you are entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element? (the case of a further assessment)
      `before 6 April 2026 I had limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day before 6 April 2026 did you have limited capability for work and work-related activity?
      `before 6 April 2026 my award did not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day before 6 April 2026 did your award not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (the relevant period)?
      `on or after 6 April 2026 the LCWRA element was included in my award` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day on or after 6 April 2026 was the LCWRA element included in your award of universal credit?
      `before 6 April 2026 I was entitled to an employment and support allowance that included the support component` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a day before 6 April 2026 were you entitled to an employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 that includes the support component?
      `I have been so entitled throughout from 6 April 2026 to the date I was awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you been so entitled throughout the period beginning with 6 April 2026 and ending with the date you were awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a pre-2026 claimant for the LCWRA element` IF
    `Sch 5A para 1 — the claimant is a pre-2026 claimant` `me as a possible pre-2026 claimant`
    WHERE
        `me as a possible pre-2026 claimant` MEANS `Claimant who may be a pre-2026 claimant` WITH
            capability IS `Capability for work` WITH
                `limited capability for work` IS TRUE
                `limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `I have limited capability for work and work-related activity`
                `severe conditions criteria claimant` IS FALSE
            `the claimant is entitled to an award of universal credit that includes the LCWRA element` IS `my award of universal credit includes the LCWRA element`
            `the claimant has been so entitled continuously from the time that the LCWRA element was included in the award` IS `I have been so entitled continuously since the LCWRA element was included`
            `circumstances of paragraph 2` IS `Claimant awaiting an assessment under Part 5` WITH
                `a day before 6th April 2026 on which, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(a), the claimant was awaiting an assessment under Part 5` IS `uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` `before 6 April 2026 I was awaiting an assessment under Part 5 (regulation 41(1)(a))`
                `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element` IS `uc3 seat — a day on or after 6 April 2026 if there was one` `on or after 6 April 2026 I was found to have LCWRA and entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element (case 2)`
                `the route by which that decision is made` IS `some other route`
            `circumstances of paragraph 3` IS `Claimant with limited capability for work awaiting a further assessment` WITH
                `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant had limited capability for work` IS `uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` `before 6 April 2026 I had limited capability for work`
                `a day before 6th April 2026 on which, in accordance with regulation 41(1)(b), the claimant was awaiting a further assessment under Part 5` IS `uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` `before 6 April 2026 I was awaiting a further assessment under Part 5 (regulation 41(1)(b))`
                `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the claimant is determined to have limited capability for work and work-related activity and a decision is made that the claimant is entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element` IS `uc3 seat — a day on or after 6 April 2026 if there was one` `on or after 6 April 2026 I was found to have LCWRA and entitled to an award that includes the LCWRA element (case 3)`
                `the route by which that decision is made` IS `some other route`
            `circumstances of paragraph 4` IS `Claimant whose award does not include the LCWRA element on 6th April 2026` WITH
                `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant had limited capability for work and work-related activity` IS `uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` `before 6 April 2026 I had limited capability for work and work-related activity`
                `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant's award did not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1) (relevant period)` IS `uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` `before 6 April 2026 my award did not include the LCWRA element by virtue of regulation 28(1)`
                `the day on or after 6th April 2026 on which the LCWRA element is included in the claimant's award of universal credit` IS `uc3 seat — a day on or after 6 April 2026 if there was one` `on or after 6 April 2026 the LCWRA element was included in my award`
            `circumstances of paragraph 5` IS `Claimant entitled to an employment and support allowance before 6th April 2026` WITH
                `a day before 6th April 2026 on which the claimant was entitled to an employment and support allowance under Part 1 of the Welfare Reform Act 2007 that includes the support component within the meaning of that Part` IS `uc3 seat — a day before 6 April 2026 if there was one` `before 6 April 2026 I was entitled to an employment and support allowance that included the support component`
                `the claimant has been so entitled throughout the period beginning with 6th April 2026 and ending with the date on which the claimant is awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element` IS `I have been so entitled throughout from 6 April 2026 to the date I was awarded universal credit that includes the LCWRA element`
